-- careers-in-ibm-usa-20261125 (usa; USA; verifiedAt 2026-11-25)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'careers-in-ibm-usa-20261125', 'usa', 'USA',
'Careers in IBM USA: Developer Roles Pay Up to $212,000',
'Careers in IBM USA: Developer Roles Pay Up to $212,000',
'Careers in IBM USA are open for developers, including an Application Developer in Herndon at $114,000 to $212,000 and Dallas roles at up to $167,000.',
'Careers in IBM USA are open for developers, including an Application Developer in Herndon at $114,000 to $212,000 and Dallas roles at up to $167,000.',
$$<p>IBM are hiring application developers across the US with hybrid roles available in Virginia, Texas, California and Arizona. Careers in IBM USA in this roundup pay from $89,000 to $212,000 a year, and the listings checked state there is no fixed closing date.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>IBM (International Business Machines Corporation)</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Application Developer, Open Source; Application Developer, Experience Front End; Application Developer, Java and Web Technologies</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$89,000 to $212,000 a year, depending on the role and location</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Posted 16 to 18 November 2026; no closing date stated</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through IBM Careers</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Degree in computer science or a related field, plus relevant development experience</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application and interview; travel of up to 80% applies to some posts</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What careers in IBM USA involve</h2><p>IBM's application developers design, build and support software for clients all over the US. The Open Source developer in Herndon, VA is an open source software engineering role in a hybrid arrangement. The Experience Front End developer in Dallas is focused on front end experience work. The Java and Web Technologies developer in San Jose is working on data and analytics. All of these are regular full time roles and several of them require up to 80% travel (four days a week) with weekends at home depending on the project. IBM is a global technology company with businesses in mainframes, cloud, consulting and AI. For readers looking at other <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> we've also got a report on the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/affirm-software-engineer-jobs-remote-20261123">Affirm software engineer jobs</a> which is another US tech employer that is hiring remotely.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>The posts are for professional developers with a degree and relevant experience in front end, back end or full stack. The Dallas and San Jose posts are hybrid (part time in the office), the Herndon post is also hybrid. There will be a significant amount of travel on some of the posts so applicants should look at the travel line on each listing. IBM's own careers site and the job numbers (143803, 143884 and 145334) will be the identifiers on that site. Glassdoor reported 37 open IBM US jobs in November 2026.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The Open Source developer in Herndon pays $114,000 to $212,000 a year, the highest earner in this roundup. The developers in Dallas, San Jose and Tempe developer posts each pay a projected $89,000 to $167,000 a year. These are the projected min and max salaries as stated in the IBM posting text. Actual pay will vary depending on the individual's skills, experience and location. Glassdoor's employee reported figures put IBM software engineer median total pay at $147,271 a year and application developer is $127,770 which are within the ranges above.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply via IBM Careers by searching for the job number or role title. The Herndon posting was dated 16th November 2026, the Dallas one 17th November and the San Jose one 18th November. None of the posts have a closing date so they may close when filled. Your application should clearly indicate the specific stack and delivery experience required in each posting and be truthful about your availability to travel where that is required.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>There's no closing date on any of the listings checked, no interview dates or start dates are given and there's no indication of how many posts are available for each role. None of the listings state whether visa sponsorship is available so international applicants should check the live IBM posting prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> IBM Careers applications are free and IBM will never ask you to pay anything in order to apply, to take part in an assessment or to receive a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.theladders.com/job/application-developer-open-source-ibm-virginia-mn_89918535?source=company">The Ladders</a> (the IBM Application Developer, Open Source listing: posting date, job number and salary range); <a href="https://jobs.codemind.site/jobs/application-developer-experience-front-end-ibm-6affcc4caa4e7eef544cc207">CodeMind Jobs</a> (the IBM Application Developer, Experience Front End listing as published: salary and travel); <a href="https://jobs.codemind.site/jobs/application-developer-java-web-technologies-ibm-6affcc4baa4e7eef544cc115">CodeMind Jobs</a> (the IBM Application Developer, Java and Web Technologies listing as published: salary and location).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the best paid IBM role?</h3><p>The Application Developer, Open Source, in Herndon, Virginia, at $114,000 to $212,000 a year.</p><h3>When do applications close?</h3><p>There's no closing date on any of the roles we've checked so they could well close when filled.</p><h3>Are those IBM roles remote?</h3><p>No, they're hybrid roles with some in the office and some requiring up to 80% travel.</p><h3>Where do I apply?</h3><p>Apply via IBM Careers using the job number from the advert (e.g. 143803 for the Herndon post).</p>
$$,
