-- jobs-in-cognizant-usa-20261125 (usa; USA; verifiedAt 2026-11-25)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'jobs-in-cognizant-usa-20261125', 'usa', 'USA',
'Jobs in Cognizant USA: Roles Pay Up to $218,000',
'Jobs in Cognizant USA: Roles Pay Up to $218,000',
'Jobs in Cognizant USA are open now, including a Transformation Lead paying $140,000 to $160,000 and an AI engineer role at up to $158,500.',
'Jobs in Cognizant USA are open now, including a Transformation Lead paying $140,000 to $160,000 and an AI engineer role at up to $158,500.',
$$<p>Cognizant are hiring across the US for AI, cloud and consulting roles with a number of positions closing at the end of November. Jobs in Cognizant USA in this round are paying from $115,000 to $218,000 a year, and applications close between 29th and 30th November 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Cognizant</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Transformation Lead, AI Forward Deployed Engineer, ML / Applied Scientist, Director of Utilities Consulting</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$115,000 to $218,000 a year, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Applications accepted until 29 to 30 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through Cognizant Careers</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Relevant degree and experience in AI, cloud, machine learning or utilities consulting</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application and interview; salary depends on experience and location</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in Cognizant USA involve</h2><p>The Transformation Lead in Irvine, CA is responsible for driving enterprise transformation in the areas of AI, automation and cloud modernisation with a focus on improving operational efficiency and delivering tangible outcomes for clients. The role is hybrid, requiring three days in client or Cognizant office). The AI Forward Deployed Engineer is a remote US role and works directly with the client to deploy AI. The ML / Applied Scientist is also a remote US role and is responsible for building ML models for entity resolution, inference and intelligent data classification. The Director in the Utilities Consulting Practice leads the energy and utilities consulting work from there, with GIS experience required. For those looking at other <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a>, there's a guide out there on <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/software-engineer-jobs-in-usa-for-foreigners-h-1b-pay-and-hiring-guide-20261029">software engineer jobs in the USA for foreigners</a> which looks at the H-1B route into US tech work.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>These are experienced hire roles for people with proven experience in AI, machine learning, cloud and/or consulting. The Transformation Lead will need to have experience in leading large scale transformation programmes. The ML / Applied Scientist will need hands on ML experience. The Director role will require utilities consulting experience and GIS-ArcPro skills. Cognizant state that for any of the US roles applicants must be currently authorised to work for any employer in the US and the Director role specifically states that the applicant must be legally authorised to work in the US at the time of application (i.e. no employer sponsorship required now or in the future). Separately Cognizant have a plan to hire 1,500 US college graduates by the end of 2026 via their graduate programmes, apprenticeships and engineering initiatives.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p> Director, Utilities Consulting Practice, pays the most in this roundup, at $137,250 to $218,000 a year. The Transformation Lead pays $140,000 to $160,000, the AI Forward Deployed Engineer $130,000 to $158,500, and the ML / Applied Scientist $115,000 to $130,000. Cognizant states the salary information is accurate as of the date of posting and may be changed at any time in accordance with applicable law. Performance based incentives are offered and the benefits package includes a 401k with company match and health care.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply via Cognizant Careers (search by role title or job number on the listing). Applications for the Transformation Lead and the ML/Applied Scientist role will be accepted until 29th November 2026. Applications for the AI Forward Deployed Engineer and the Director role will be accepted until 30th November 2026. Applications must include tangible evidence of delivery in the areas of AI, cloud or consulting with where possible some form of measurable outcome.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings make no mention of how many posts are available for each role, nor do they give any interview or start dates. They provide no breakdown of pay by location other than to state that pay is dependent on experience, qualifications, geographic location and skills. The listings and two explicitly state that applicants must already be authorised to work in the US.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> Cognizant Careers applications are free and Cognizant will never ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://careers.cognizant.com/global-en/jobs/00071323971/transformation-lead-ai-automation-cloud-modernization/">Cognizant Careers</a> (Transformation Lead listing: salary, location and closing date); <a href="https://careers.cognizant.com/global-en/jobs/00069909832/ai-forward-deployed-engineer/">Cognizant Careers</a> (AI Forward Deployed Engineer listing: salary and closing date); <a href="http://careers.cognizant.com/india-en/jobs/00070902531/ml-applied-scientist/">Cognizant Careers</a> (ML / Applied Scientist listing: salary and closing date).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the highest paying Cognizant role?</h3><p>The Director, Utilities Consulting Practice, at $137,250 to $218,000 a year.</p><h3>When do applications close?</h3><p>29th November 2026 for the Transformation Lead and ML / Applied Scientist, and 30th November for the AI Forward Deployed Engineer and Director.</p><h3>Are any of those roles remote?</h3><p>Yes. The AI Forward Deployed Engineer and ML / Applied Scientist are remote roles open to qualified US based applicants.</p><h3>Does Cognizant sponsor visas for these roles?</h3><p>The listings don't have any sponsorship and two state that the applicant must already be authorised to work in the US.</p>
$$,
$$<p>Cognizant are hiring across the US for AI, cloud and consulting roles with a number of positions closing at the end of November. Jobs in Cognizant USA in this round are paying from $115,000 to $218,000 a year, and applications close between 29th and 30th November 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Cognizant</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Transformation Lead, AI Forward Deployed Engineer, ML / Applied Scientist, Director of Utilities Consulting</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$115,000 to $218,000 a year, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Applications accepted until 29 to 30 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through Cognizant Careers</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Relevant degree and experience in AI, cloud, machine learning or utilities consulting</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application and interview; salary depends on experience and location</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in Cognizant USA involve</h2><p>The Transformation Lead in Irvine, CA is responsible for driving enterprise transformation in the areas of AI, automation and cloud modernisation with a focus on improving operational efficiency and delivering tangible outcomes for clients. The role is hybrid, requiring three days in client or Cognizant office). The AI Forward Deployed Engineer is a remote US role and works directly with the client to deploy AI. The ML / Applied Scientist is also a remote US role and is responsible for building ML models for entity resolution, inference and intelligent data classification. The Director in the Utilities Consulting Practice leads the energy and utilities consulting work from there, with GIS experience required. For those looking at other <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a>, there's a guide out there on <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/software-engineer-jobs-in-usa-for-foreigners-h-1b-pay-and-hiring-guide-20261029">software engineer jobs in the USA for foreigners</a> which looks at the H-1B route into US tech work.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>These are experienced hire roles for people with proven experience in AI, machine learning, cloud and/or consulting. The Transformation Lead will need to have experience in leading large scale transformation programmes. The ML / Applied Scientist will need hands on ML experience. The Director role will require utilities consulting experience and GIS-ArcPro skills. Cognizant state that for any of the US roles applicants must be currently authorised to work for any employer in the US and the Director role specifically states that the applicant must be legally authorised to work in the US at the time of application (i.e. no employer sponsorship required now or in the future). Separately Cognizant have a plan to hire 1,500 US college graduates by the end of 2026 via their graduate programmes, apprenticeships and engineering initiatives.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p> Director, Utilities Consulting Practice, pays the most in this roundup, at $137,250 to $218,000 a year. The Transformation Lead pays $140,000 to $160,000, the AI Forward Deployed Engineer $130,000 to $158,500, and the ML / Applied Scientist $115,000 to $130,000. Cognizant states the salary information is accurate as of the date of posting and may be changed at any time in accordance with applicable law. Performance based incentives are offered and the benefits package includes a 401k with company match and health care.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply via Cognizant Careers (search by role title or job number on the listing). Applications for the Transformation Lead and the ML/Applied Scientist role will be accepted until 29th November 2026. Applications for the AI Forward Deployed Engineer and the Director role will be accepted until 30th November 2026. Applications must include tangible evidence of delivery in the areas of AI, cloud or consulting with where possible some form of measurable outcome.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings make no mention of how many posts are available for each role, nor do they give any interview or start dates. They provide no breakdown of pay by location other than to state that pay is dependent on experience, qualifications, geographic location and skills. The listings and two explicitly state that applicants must already be authorised to work in the US.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> Cognizant Careers applications are free and Cognizant will never ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://careers.cognizant.com/global-en/jobs/00071323971/transformation-lead-ai-automation-cloud-modernization/">Cognizant Careers</a> (Transformation Lead listing: salary, location and closing date); <a href="https://careers.cognizant.com/global-en/jobs/00069909832/ai-forward-deployed-engineer/">Cognizant Careers</a> (AI Forward Deployed Engineer listing: salary and closing date); <a href="http://careers.cognizant.com/india-en/jobs/00070902531/ml-applied-scientist/">Cognizant Careers</a> (ML / Applied Scientist listing: salary and closing date).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the highest paying Cognizant role?</h3><p>The Director, Utilities Consulting Practice, at $137,250 to $218,000 a year.</p><h3>When do applications close?</h3><p>29th November 2026 for the Transformation Lead and ML / Applied Scientist, and 30th November for the AI Forward Deployed Engineer and Director.</p><h3>Are any of those roles remote?</h3><p>Yes. The AI Forward Deployed Engineer and ML / Applied Scientist are remote roles open to qualified US based applicants.</p><h3>Does Cognizant sponsor visas for these roles?</h3><p>The listings don't have any sponsorship and two state that the applicant must already be authorised to work in the US.</p>
$$,
ARRAY['https://careers.cognizant.com/global-en/jobs/00071323971/transformation-lead-ai-automation-cloud-modernization/', 'https://careers.cognizant.com/global-en/jobs/00069909832/ai-forward-deployed-engineer/', 'http://careers.cognizant.com/india-en/jobs/00070902531/ml-applied-scientist/'], NOW(), NOW(), NOW(), '2026-11-25'::timestamptz, NULL) ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

-- jobs-in-connecticut-usa-20261125 (usa; USA; verifiedAt 2026-11-25)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'jobs-in-connecticut-usa-20261125', 'usa', 'USA',
'Jobs in Connecticut USA: State Roles Pay Up to $133,870',
'Jobs in Connecticut USA: State Roles Pay Up to $133,870',
'Jobs in Connecticut USA are open in state government, including a Staff Attorney at up to $133,870 and an Associate Accountant at up to $122,027.',
'Jobs in Connecticut USA are open in state government, including a Staff Attorney at up to $133,870 and an Associate Accountant at up to $122,027.',
$$<p>Connecticut state government is hiring in Hartford with finance, legal and technology roles available across the various departments. Jobs in Connecticut USA in this roundup pay from $87,787 to $133,870 per year and the earliest live closing date is 30th November 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>State of Connecticut, Departments of Social Services and Energy and Environmental Protection</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Associate Accountant, Staff Attorney 2, Human Resources Generalist 2</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$87,787 to $133,870 a year, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Closing 30 November to 3 December 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the State of Connecticut Online Employment Center</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Relevant degree and experience for each role; law degree and bar admission for the attorney post</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application and assessment; new state employees start at the minimum salary</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in Connecticut USA involve</h2><p>DOSS is hiring an Associate Accountant in its Fiscal Services Division (Hartford) in the General Accounting Unit to work on the financials of the state's health and human services programmes. The DEEP is seeking a Staff Attorney 2 in its Office of Legal Counsel to advise the Commissioner on environmental law. DAS is also hiring Human Resources Generalist 2 staff to work with the Department of Correction, with positions in Brooklyn, Montville and Newtown. State positions are Monday to Friday and the accountant position is hybrid. Readers looking at other <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> can also take a look at our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/cleaning-jobs-in-usa-for-foreigners-pay-roles-and-how-to-apply-20261030">cleaning jobs in the USA for foreigners</a> which looks at the entry level opportunities available with very different requirements.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p> Associate Accountant: suitable for a hard-working, detail oriented applicant with accounting experience and a relevant qualification. Staff Attorney 2: requires a law degree and admission to practise, with experience in environmental or administrative law being an advantage. The Human Resources Generalist 2 posts are for experienced HR people who can provide on-site agency support. All three of these are open to the public. The state also notes that for current state employees, the salary calculations are not necessarily comparable across the Executive, Legislative and Judicial branches. Connecticut is an eligible Public Service Loan Forgiveness employer so qualifying employees may have their student loans forgiven after ten years of service.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The Staff Attorney 2 pays $104,612 to $133,870 a year, and the Associate Accountant pays $94,882 to $122,027 a year. The Human Resources Generalist 2 pays $87,787 to $119,701 a year. New state employees start at the minimum of the range in each case. State employees receive health and retirement benefits, paid holidays, vacation and sick leave, three paid personal days a year, group life insurance and a 457 deferred compensation plan.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply only via the 'Apply' or 'Apply Online' buttons on the official State of Connecticut Online Employment Centre job advert as the State stresses in each advert. The Associate Accountant closes at 11.59pm on 30th November 2026 and the Staff Attorney 2 closes at 11.59pm on 3rd December 2026. Must be a complete application by the close of the advert and any questions regarding a recruitment should be directed to the contact details provided on the advert.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings don't state how many posts are available for each role and give no interview dates or start dates. The Judicial Branch tech role which was in the $111,858 to $148,027 bracket had a deadline of 23 November 2026 which has now passed so it's not included in the above. None of the listings indicate whether visa sponsorship is available so international applicants should check directly with the hiring agency prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> State of Connecticut applications are free and no state agency will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.onetonline.org/link/jobinfo?id=3A3B516CF5B349AFB34A9326234AFB85206">O*NET Online</a> (Associate Accountant listing as published: salary, location and closing date); <a href="https://www.onetonline.org/link/jobinfo?id=9C0A2DAD51C742C4813F6DBA0927F9A5206">O*NET Online</a> (Staff Attorney 2 listing as published: salary, location and closing date); <a href="http://www.jud.ct.gov/jobs/JobDetails.aspx?j=8075">Connecticut Judicial Branch</a> (Information Technology Analyst III posting: salary and deadline).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the best paid role in Connecticut?</h3><p>The Staff Attorney 2 at the Department of Energy and Environmental Protection, at $104,612 to $133,870 a year.</p><h3>When do applications close?</h3><p> Associate Accountant position closes 30th November 2026. Staff Attorney 2 position closes 3rd December 2026.</p><h3>Where are the roles based?</h3><p>Hartford for the accountant and attorney posts and Brooklyn, Montville and Newtown for the HR roles.</p><h3>Do new state employees start at the top of the pay range?</h3><p>No. The listings state that employees new to state service start at the minimum of the range.</p>
$$,
