hich has now passed so it's not included in the above. None of the listings indicate whether visa sponsorship is available so international applicants should check directly with the hiring agency prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> State of Connecticut applications are free and no state agency will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.onetonline.org/link/jobinfo?id=3A3B516CF5B349AFB34A9326234AFB85206">O*NET Online</a> (Associate Accountant listing as published: salary, location and closing date); <a href="https://www.onetonline.org/link/jobinfo?id=9C0A2DAD51C742C4813F6DBA0927F9A5206">O*NET Online</a> (Staff Attorney 2 listing as published: salary, location and closing date); <a href="http://www.jud.ct.gov/jobs/JobDetails.aspx?j=8075">Connecticut Judicial Branch</a> (Information Technology Analyst III posting: salary and deadline).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the best paid role in Connecticut?</h3><p>The Staff Attorney 2 at the Department of Energy and Environmental Protection, at $104,612 to $133,870 a year.</p><h3>When do applications close?</h3><p> Associate Accountant position closes 30th November 2026. Staff Attorney 2 position closes 3rd December 2026.</p><h3>Where are the roles based?</h3><p>Hartford for the accountant and attorney posts and Brooklyn, Montville and Newtown for the HR roles.</p><h3>Do new state employees start at the top of the pay range?</h3><p>No. The listings state that employees new to state service start at the minimum of the range.</p>
