r each role. None of the adverts checked confirm visa sponsorship, so international applicants should check the live Google Careers advert before applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> Google Careers applications are free and Google will never ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://roleweek.com/job/staff-software-engineer-ai-ml-genai-google-workspace-google-san-francisco-bay-area-aaf4bfe2/">RoleWeek</a> (the Google Staff Software Engineer listing from the employer's job board: pay, locations and posting date); <a href="https://roleweek.com/job/senior-business-data-scientist-google-cloud-google-san-francisco-bay-area-cb2f46c5/">RoleWeek</a> (the Google Senior Business Data Scientist listing from the employer's job board: pay and posting date); <a href="https://www.codingjobboard.com/job/staff-software-engineer-at-google-usa/31740">Coding Job Board</a> (the Google Staff Software Engineer listing as published: pay and benefits).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the highest paying Google job?</h3><p>Staff Software Engineer, AI/ML GenAI, at $207,000 to $300,000 in base plus 20% bonus target, equity and benefits.</p><h3>When do applications close?</h3><p>There's no closing date on the Google ads that we checked so the roles could well close when filled.</p><h3>Where are these Google roles based?</h3><p>Sunnyvale, Mountain View, San Jose and San Francisco in California and New York.</p><h3>Are these roles for new grads?</h3><p>No, these are experienced hires. The staff engineer role is specifically looking for eight or more years' experience.</p>
