-- jobs-in-kentucky-usa-20261125 (usa; USA; verifiedAt 2026-11-25)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'jobs-in-kentucky-usa-20261125', 'usa', 'USA',
'Jobs in Kentucky USA: State Roles Close 27 November',
'Jobs in Kentucky USA: State Roles Close 27 November',
'Jobs in Kentucky USA are open in state government, including an Administrative Specialist at up to $54,639 and a Correctional Officer at $39,128.',
'Jobs in Kentucky USA are open in state government, including an Administrative Specialist at up to $54,639 and a Correctional Officer at $39,128.',
$$<p>Kentucky state government is recruiting in Frankfort and across the state's correctional facilities with a number of office, legal and enforcement positions now open. Jobs in Kentucky USA listed here pay between $39,128 and $65,452 per year with the earliest closing date being 27th November 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Commonwealth of Kentucky, Cabinets for Health and Family Services and Justice and Public Safety</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Administrative Specialist, Workers Compensation Specialist, Correctional Officer</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$39,128 to $65,452 a year, depending on the role, plus premiums for correctional staff</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Closing 27 to 28 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the Kentucky personnel careers site</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Relevant experience for each role; background checks for health and corrections posts</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application and assessment; six-month probationary period for some posts</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in Kentucky USA involve</h2><p>The Department for Community Based Services is hiring an Administrative Specialist in Frankfort to work on family self-sufficiency and child and vulnerable adult safety and permanency for children and vulnerable adults. The Department of Workers' Claims is seeking a Workers Compensation Specialist in its Office of Administrative Law Judges in Frankfort to administer claims under Kentucky workers' compensation law. The Department of Corrections is hiring Correctional Officers at West Liberty, Central City, Burgin, Pewee Valley and Eddyville. The officers will work as a team to maintain safety and control. The Kentucky Council on Postsecondary Education has a Senior Associate position for workforce and economic development in Frankfort at $60,000 to $72,000, though that position has a priority deadline of 23 November 2026. Anyone looking at other <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> can also check out our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/warehouse-jobs-in-usa-for-foreigners-visa-pay-and-how-to-apply-20261025">warehouse jobs in the USA for foreigners</a> which looks at another major route into the American workforce.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p> Administrative Specialist is a role for a driven applicant who wants to be able to help vulnerable people. It's a full time role at 37.5 hours per week. The Workers' Compensation Specialist is a 37.5 hour per week role in Frankfort and must be able to do the job in Kentucky. Correctional Officers are 40 hours per week and will be required to pass the appropriate checks that apply to justice roles. Applicants for the health and family services post must submit to a fingerprint based criminal background check via the Kentucky State Police and the Federal Bureau of the posts will have employees who are prohibited from using medical cannabis despite it being legal in the state due to other applicable laws.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The Workers Compensation Specialist makes $4,040.24 to $5,454.32 per month (i.e. $48,483 to $65,452 per annum). The Administrative Specialist makes $48,221.92 to $54,639.12 per annum at pay grade 12. The Correctional Officer makes $39,127.68 per annum at pay grade 10 plus a locality premium of $5.23 an hour and shift, weekend and holiday premiums of $2.13 an hour each. The posts are full time, eligible for overtime and carry state employee benefits.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply online via the Kentucky Personnel Careers site by searching for the advert number on each listing. The Administrative Specialist (advert 2606198) and the Workers Compensation Specialist (advert 2606202) both close at 11.59pm ET on 27th November 2026. The Correctional Officer post in West Liberty (advert 2606216) closes at 11.59pm ET on 28th November 2026, the other Correctional Officer adverts having closed on the 22nd and 23rd respectively. Queries should be directed to the contact details provided on each advert.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings don't state how many posts are open for each position, nor do they give any interview dates or start dates. They don't state the total number of Correctional Officer vacancies across the state's institutions. None of the listings as to whether visa sponsorship is available so international applicants should check directly with the hiring agency prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> Commonwealth of Kentucky applications are free and no state agency will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.onetonline.org/link/jobinfo?id=CAC1E7EB8354434FB27775353757E186206">O*NET Online</a> (Administrative Specialist listing as published: salary, location and closing date); <a href="https://www.onetonline.org/link/jobinfo?id=92FE6EB38551480193C9A61E57486C0B206">O*NET Online</a> (Workers Compensation Specialist listing as published: salary and closing date); <a href="http://cpe.ky.gov/news/jobs/workforce-srassociate-cdo.html">Kentucky Council on Postsecondary Education</a> (Senior Associate posting: salary and priority deadline).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>When do these Kentucky applications close?</h3><p>On 27 November 2026 for the Administrative Specialist and Workers Compensation Specialist, and on 28 November for the West Liberty Correctional Officer post.</p><h3>What does a Correctional Officer earn in Kentucky?</h3><p>$39,127.68 a year, plus a $5.23-an-hour locality premium and $2.13-an-hour shift, weekend and holiday premiums.</p><h3>What's the highest paid job in this list?</h3><p>The Workers Compensation Specialist, at $4,040.24 to $5,454.32 a month.</p><h3>Do these posts need a background check?</h3><p>Yes, the Health and Family Services post has a criminal record check via fingerprint and the Corrections posts have their own checks.</p>
$$,
$$<p>Kentucky state government is recruiting in Frankfort and across the state's correctional facilities with a number of office, legal and enforcement positions now open. Jobs in Kentucky USA listed here pay between $39,128 and $65,452 per year with the earliest closing date being 27th November 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Commonwealth of Kentucky, Cabinets for Health and Family Services and Justice and Public Safety</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Administrative Specialist, Workers Compensation Specialist, Correctional Officer</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$39,128 to $65,452 a year, depending on the role, plus premiums for correctional staff</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Closing 27 to 28 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the Kentucky personnel careers site</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Relevant experience for each role; background checks for health and corrections posts</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application and assessment; six-month probationary period for some posts</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in Kentucky USA involve</h2><p>The Department for Community Based Services is hiring an Administrative Specialist in Frankfort to work on family self-sufficiency and child and vulnerable adult safety and permanency for children and vulnerable adults. The Department of Workers' Claims is seeking a Workers Compensation Specialist in its Office of Administrative Law Judges in Frankfort to administer claims under Kentucky workers' compensation law. The Department of Corrections is hiring Correctional Officers at West Liberty, Central City, Burgin, Pewee Valley and Eddyville. The officers will work as a team to maintain safety and control. The Kentucky Council on Postsecondary Education has a Senior Associate position for workforce and economic development in Frankfort at $60,000 to $72,000, though that position has a priority deadline of 23 November 2026. Anyone looking at other <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> can also check out our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/warehouse-jobs-in-usa-for-foreigners-visa-pay-and-how-to-apply-20261025">warehouse jobs in the USA for foreigners</a> which looks at another major route into the American workforce.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p> Administrative Specialist is a role for a driven applicant who wants to be able to help vulnerable people. It's a full time role at 37.5 hours per week. The Workers' Compensation Specialist is a 37.5 hour per week role in Frankfort and must be able to do the job in Kentucky. Correctional Officers are 40 hours per week and will be required to pass the appropriate checks that apply to justice roles. Applicants for the health and family services post must submit to a fingerprint based criminal background check via the Kentucky State Police and the Federal Bureau of the posts will have employees who are prohibited from using medical cannabis despite it being legal in the state due to other applicable laws.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The Workers Compensation Specialist makes $4,040.24 to $5,454.32 per month (i.e. $48,483 to $65,452 per annum). The Administrative Specialist makes $48,221.92 to $54,639.12 per annum at pay grade 12. The Correctional Officer makes $39,127.68 per annum at pay grade 10 plus a locality premium of $5.23 an hour and shift, weekend and holiday premiums of $2.13 an hour each. The posts are full time, eligible for overtime and carry state employee benefits.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply online via the Kentucky Personnel Careers site by searching for the advert number on each listing. The Administrative Specialist (advert 2606198) and the Workers Compensation Specialist (advert 2606202) both close at 11.59pm ET on 27th November 2026. The Correctional Officer post in West Liberty (advert 2606216) closes at 11.59pm ET on 28th November 2026, the other Correctional Officer adverts having closed on the 22nd and 23rd respectively. Queries should be directed to the contact details provided on each advert.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings don't state how many posts are open for each position, nor do they give any interview dates or start dates. They don't state the total number of Correctional Officer vacancies across the state's institutions. None of the listings as to whether visa sponsorship is available so international applicants should check directly with the hiring agency prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> Commonwealth of Kentucky applications are free and no state agency will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.onetonline.org/link/jobinfo?id=CAC1E7EB8354434FB27775353757E186206">O*NET Online</a> (Administrative Specialist listing as published: salary, location and closing date); <a href="https://www.onetonline.org/link/jobinfo?id=92FE6EB38551480193C9A61E57486C0B206">O*NET Online</a> (Workers Compensation Specialist listing as published: salary and closing date); <a href="http://cpe.ky.gov/news/jobs/workforce-srassociate-cdo.html">Kentucky Council on Postsecondary Education</a> (Senior Associate posting: salary and priority deadline).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>When do these Kentucky applications close?</h3><p>On 27 November 2026 for the Administrative Specialist and Workers Compensation Specialist, and on 28 November for the West Liberty Correctional Officer post.</p><h3>What does a Correctional Officer earn in Kentucky?</h3><p>$39,127.68 a year, plus a $5.23-an-hour locality premium and $2.13-an-hour shift, weekend and holiday premiums.</p><h3>What's the highest paid job in this list?</h3><p>The Workers Compensation Specialist, at $4,040.24 to $5,454.32 a month.</p><h3>Do these posts need a background check?</h3><p>Yes, the Health and Family Services post has a criminal record check via fingerprint and the Corrections posts have their own checks.</p>
