'Jobs in Microsoft USA are open now, including a Principal Software Engineer in Redmond at $143,000 to $331,000 and a remote Copilot engineer at up to $235,000.',
$$<p>Microsoft is hiring software engineers across the United States, with senior and principal roles open in Redmond and remote posts open nationwide. Jobs in Microsoft USA in this roundup pay from $85,400 to $331,000 a year in base pay, and most posts stay open for at least five days.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Microsoft</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Principal Software Engineer, Senior Software Engineer, Software Engineer, Developer Experience Lead</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>USD $85,400 to $331,000 a year in base pay, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Open now; posts stay open for at least 5 days until filled</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through Microsoft Careers</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Relevant degree and experience; senior posts need several years of engineering work</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application and interview; some roles are not open to visa sponsorship</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in Microsoft USA involve</h2><p> Principal Software Engineer in Redmond working on the services and backend infrastructure for the AI experiences in Microsoft Edge. Senior Software Engineer/Principal Software Engineer for Copilot CLI working remotely on the Microsoft Copilot CLI. Senior Software Engineer in the Office Product Group building the AI and agentic systems underpinning the unified data platform for Office (the governed source of truth for all our experimentation and Copilot analysis). Windows and Devices Developer Experience Lead (principal Technical Programme Manager) owns the developer friction domain across Windows and devices. Software Engineer in Finance Data and Experiences in Redmond (hybrid) working on AI enabled business apps, cloud services and data analytics. If you're interested in Redmond, in a hybrid arrangement. Readers exploring other <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs then you</a> can also have a look at our report on the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/amazon-warehouse-jobs-pay-shifts-roles-and-how-to-apply-20261031">Amazon warehouse jobs</a> which is another very large US employer hiring at scale this month.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>These are all experienced hire engineering roles. The Software Engineer in Finance Data & Experiences is an IC2, the Office Product Group role is an IC4 (a senior grade). The Windows & Devices Developer Experience Lead needs expertise in hardware, OS and developer technologies and the posting makes it very clear that Microsoft cannot sponsor a work visa for that role due to the nature of the job. The Redmond roles are all hybrid or on-site (the Azure PostgreSQL software engineer post requiring three days on site), the Copilot CLI is remote. Candidates should always check the work model and sponsorship line on the live posting.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The Principal Software Engineer in Redmond pays $143,000 to $331,000 a year, the highest range in this roundup. The Windows and Devices Developer Experience Lead pays $142,800 to $274,800 across the United States, or $188,000 to $304,200 in the San Francisco Bay Area and New York City. The Senior Software Engineer in the Office Product Group pays $119,800 to $234,700, or $160,200 to $261,000 in the Bay Area and New York City. The remote Copilot CLI Engineer pays $120,000 to $235,000, and the Finance Data and Experiences Software Engineer pays $85,400 to $168,100, or $111,100 to $183,700 in the Bay Area and New York City. These are typical base pay ranges, not guaranteed offers.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply via Microsoft Careers using the role title. Microsoft state that each role will be open for a minimum of five days, with applications will be accepted on an ongoing basis until the role is filled (there is no fixed closing date to wait for). The Principal Software Engineer role was published one day prior to the 24th November 2026 check and the Office Product Group role five days prior to that so both are very current. Your applications should include the specific engineering experience required for each role.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>There's no stated closing date on any of the postings we've checked and no interview dates or start dates are given. The posts don't indicate how many posts there are for each role. Only the Windows and Devices post so international applicants should check the sponsorship line on each individual live post before they apply.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> Microsoft Careers applications are free and Microsoft will never ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://shouldapply.com/companies/microsoft">ShouldApply</a> (Microsoft open roles as counted from job boards: 11 posts passing quality checks, pay ranges and posting ages); <a href="https://cvrocket.ai/jobs/microsoft/senior-software-engineer-6eee98b1f535">CVRocket</a> (the Microsoft Senior Software Engineer listing as published: pay range and application window); <a href="https://remotive.com/remote/jobs/product/windows-devices-developer-experience-lead-6654478">Remotive</a> (the Microsoft Windows and Devices Developer Experience Lead listing: pay range and sponsorship note).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the highest paying Microsoft role?</h3><p>The Principal Software Engineer in Redmond, with base pay of $143,000 to $331,000 a year.</p><h3>When do applications close?</h3><p>There's no set closing date, each post will remain open for at least five days before being closed.</p><h3>Are any of the Microsoft roles in this round-up remote?</h3><p>Yes. The Copilot CLI engineer and the Windows and Devices Developer Experience Lead are both remote US roles.</p><h3>Does Microsoft sponsor visas for these roles?</h3><p>The Windows and Devices post says it can't sponsor a work visa; the other posts we've looked at don't mention sponsorship at all.</p>
$$,
