(gen_random_uuid(), 'jobs-in-montana-usa-20261125', 'usa', 'USA',
'Jobs in Montana USA: State Roles Pay Up to $150,675',
'Jobs in Montana USA: State Roles Pay Up to $150,675',
'Jobs in Montana USA are open across state government, including a Veterinary Diagnostic Pathologist at $150,675 and a Business Analyst at up to $66,955.',
'Jobs in Montana USA are open across state government, including a Veterinary Diagnostic Pathologist at $150,675 and a Business Analyst at up to $66,955.',
$$<p>Montana state government is recruiting across Helena, Bozeman and the state's transport districts with office, enforcement and veterinary positions now open. Jobs in Montana USA listed here range from $48,565 to $150,675 per year and the earliest closing date is 30th November 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>State of Montana, Departments of Revenue, Livestock and Fish, Wildlife and Parks</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Business Analyst 2, Criminal Investigator Captain, Veterinary Diagnostic Pathologist, Field Project Technician</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$48,565 to $150,675 a year, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Closing 30 November to 3 December 2026; the pathologist post is open until filled</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the State of Montana careers site</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Relevant degree and experience for each role; POST certification for the investigator captain</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application and assessment; E-Verify checks apply</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in Montana USA involve</h2><p>The Department of Revenue is hiring a Business Analyst 2 in its Information Management and Collections Division in Helena, working on the systems behind almost 40 state taxes, property appraisals and cannabis laws. The Department of Fish, Wildlife and Parks needs a Criminal Investigator Captain in Helena to supervise its Criminal Investigation Section and report directly to the Chief of Enforcement. The Department of Livestock is seeking a Veterinary Diagnostic Pathologist to lead a section of the Montana Veterinary Diagnostic Laboratory in Bozeman, a full-service laboratory accredited by the American Association of Veterinary Laboratory Diagnosticians. The Department of Transportation is also recruiting Field Project Technicians in Wolf Point, Glasgow, and Glendive to inspect construction work and materials on state road projects. Readers weighing other <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> can also read our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/farm-worker-jobs-in-usa-h-2a-visa-pay-housing-and-legal-guide-20261028">farm worker jobs in the USA</a>, which covers seasonal and visa-backed routes into rural American work.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>The Business Analyst role is open to applicants with experience in business analysis and information systems; the Department of Revenue says it will teach all computer systems and tax guidelines on the job. The Criminal Investigator Captain is a POST-certified position, and candidates need Montana certification or an equivalent from another state. The pathologist post requires a diagnostic anatomic pathologist, and applications go through the State of Montana careers website. The Field Project Technician roles run on a career ladder from Level 1 at $23.46 an hour to Junior Engineering Coordinator at $31.49 an hour. Montana state agencies participate in E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The Veterinary Diagnostic Pathologist pays $150,675 a year, the highest figure in this roundup. The Criminal Investigator Captain pays $92,456 a year, or $44.45 an hour. The Business Analyst 2 pays $64,780 to $66,955 a year, and other Department of Revenue openings listed alongside it pay $48,565 to $50,064 and $68,290 to $70,611 a year. Field Project Technicians earn $23.46 to $31.49 an hour, depending on level. State employees receive health coverage, paid leave and holidays, and a choice between two retirement plans with an employer contribution of 8.73% to 9.07% of salary.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply via the State of Montana careers site (search by title). The Criminal Investigator Captain closes at 11.59pm MT on 30 November 2026 and the Business Analyst 2 closes on 3 December 2026. The Pathologist position is open until filled with a first review of applicants on 13 November 2026 (so later applicants will be part of a rolling review). The Department of Revenue has a resume as an additional requirement for some of its positions and their HR team can be contacted at dorhr@mt.gov.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings do not say how many Field Project Technician posts are open, and the Department of Revenue page does not give a post count for every opening. No interview dates or start dates are stated. None of the listings state whether visa sponsorship is available, so international applicants should check directly with the hiring agency before applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> State of Montana applications are free and no state agency will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://revenue.mt.gov/career/">Montana Department of Revenue</a> (official careers page: Business Analyst salary, locations and closing dates); <a href="https://aylagov.com/jobs/business-analyst-2-state-of-montana-mt/632ddec7-3740-4b89-b52e-babe12e5cf7d">Ayla Government Jobs</a> (Business Analyst 2 listing as published: pay, posting date and duties); <a href="https://aylagov.com/jobs/criminal-investigator-captain-state-of-montana-mt/5af2f9b6-22f5-4e8c-b33d-3ea947855094">Ayla Government Jobs</a> (Criminal Investigator Captain listing: pay, closing date and certification requirement).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the highest paid role in Montana in this list?</h3><p>The Veterinary Diagnostic Pathologist at the Department of Livestock, at $150,675 per annum.</p><h3>When do applications close?</h3><p>The Criminal Investigator Captain closes on 30th November 2026 and the Business Analyst 2 on 3rd December 2026. The Pathologist post is open until filled.</p><h3>Where are the roles based?</h3><p>Helena for Revenue and Fish, Wildlife and Parks; Bozeman for the pathologist; Wolf Point, Glasgow and Glendive for the transport technicians.</p><h3>Do Montana state jobs offer telework?</h3><p> Revenue roles are telework eligible with supervisor approval (full time telework is not available). Investigator and pathologist roles are not telework eligible.</p>
$$,
