f a rolling review). The Department of Revenue has a resume as an additional requirement for some of its positions and their HR team can be contacted at dorhr@mt.gov.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings do not say how many Field Project Technician posts are open, and the Department of Revenue page does not give a post count for every opening. No interview dates or start dates are stated. None of the listings state whether visa sponsorship is available, so international applicants should check directly with the hiring agency before applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> State of Montana applications are free and no state agency will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://revenue.mt.gov/career/">Montana Department of Revenue</a> (official careers page: Business Analyst salary, locations and closing dates); <a href="https://aylagov.com/jobs/business-analyst-2-state-of-montana-mt/632ddec7-3740-4b89-b52e-babe12e5cf7d">Ayla Government Jobs</a> (Business Analyst 2 listing as published: pay, posting date and duties); <a href="https://aylagov.com/jobs/criminal-investigator-captain-state-of-montana-mt/5af2f9b6-22f5-4e8c-b33d-3ea947855094">Ayla Government Jobs</a> (Criminal Investigator Captain listing: pay, closing date and certification requirement).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the highest paid role in Montana in this list?</h3><p>The Veterinary Diagnostic Pathologist at the Department of Livestock, at $150,675 per annum.</p><h3>When do applications close?</h3><p>The Criminal Investigator Captain closes on 30th November 2026 and the Business Analyst 2 on 3rd December 2026. The Pathologist post is open until filled.</p><h3>Where are the roles based?</h3><p>Helena for Revenue and Fish, Wildlife and Parks; Bozeman for the pathologist; Wolf Point, Glasgow and Glendive for the transport technicians.</p><h3>Do Montana state jobs offer telework?</h3><p> Revenue roles are telework eligible with supervisor approval (full time telework is not available). Investigator and pathologist roles are not telework eligible.</p>
$$,
