(gen_random_uuid(), 'jobs-in-nestle-usa-20261125', 'usa', 'USA',
'Jobs in Nestle USA: Roles Pay Up to $146,533',
'Jobs in Nestle USA: Roles Pay Up to $146,533',
'Jobs in Nestle USA are open across the country, including a Senior Compensation Analyst at $106,444 to $146,533 and warehouse roles at $27.45 an hour.',
'Jobs in Nestle USA are open across the country, including a Senior Compensation Analyst at $106,444 to $146,533 and warehouse roles at $27.45 an hour.',
$$<p>Nestle USA are hiring across factory, warehouse, office and remote roles with hundreds of positions listed on their careers site. The jobs in Nestle USA listed here pay from $27.45 an hour to $178,443 a year and the listings checked all state no fixed closing date.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Nestle USA</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Senior Compensation Analyst, Warehouse Operator, HR Coordinator, Data System Specialist, Senior Quality Manager</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$27.45 an hour to $178,443 a year, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Open now; no closing date stated on the listings checked</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through Nestle Careers</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Relevant experience for each role; degree for the analyst and specialist posts</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application and interview; some roles are not eligible for visa sponsorship</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in Nestle USA involve</h2><p> Senior Compensation Analyst works in a client facing role with HR partners to drive pay for performance and ensure pay is fair across the business. The Warehouse Operator in the Pizza Division at Little Chute, WI does the moving of product through the warehouse on first shift. The HR Coordinator is the person who keeps the day to day HR operations running at a Nestle site, helping create a positive employee experience. The Hybrid Data System Specialist in Solon, OH supports the application systems and the Senior Quality Manager Expert works remotely with up to 70% travel to the food manufacturing sites to lead on quality and co-manufacturing. Nestle USA says all of its people work towards the same objective which is to delight and deliver for the consumer. If you're looking at other <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> then you might be interested in our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/restaurant-jobs-in-usa-for-foreigners-roles-pay-and-h-2b-guide-20261030">restaurant jobs in the USA for foreigners</a> which looks at the various routes with different visa rules that apply.</p><h2>Who can apply Analyst and Specialist roles are for the experienced professional with the relevant degree and experience.</h2><p>The warehouse role is for the doer, the hands-on type who takes pride in getting the product where it needs to be. The Senior Compensation Analyst role is very clear in that it is not eligible for visa sponsorship so that role must already authorised to work in the US. The Electro Mechanical Technician role on that same careers site works a 12 hour shift (5pm to 5am) on a 2-2-3 rota which is a very different working pattern to the others in the factories. Applicants should always check the eligibility and sponsorship line on each post.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The Senior Quality Manager Expert pays $134,664.30 to $178,443 a year, and the Senior Compensation Analyst pays $106,443.54 to $146,533 a year. The Hybrid Data System Specialist pays $82,323.90 to $107,671 a year, and the HR Coordinator $42,969.60 to $60,332 a year. The Warehouse Operator pays $27.45 an hour. Nestle says each pay range is a good-faith estimate for the position at the time of posting, and it offers performance-based incentives plus a 401(k) with company match, health care coverage, and other benefits.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply via Nestle Careers, searching for the role title or the job requisition number. The Senior Compensation Analyst is requisition 426793 and the Warehouse Operator is requisition 426966. As the listings state no closing date, the roles can close at any time when filled so applicants should apply as soon as possible and check the live listing prior to applying. Your application must meet the requirements of the role as advertised (including shift availability for the factory posts).</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>There's no closing date on any of the listings that we've checked and no interview dates or start dates are provided. The listings don't state how many posts are available for each role. The only one of the roles in this lot to state its visa status is the Senior Compensation Analyst post is the only one in this roundup that states its visa position explicitly, so sponsorship for the others is not confirmed and would need to be checked directly with Nestle prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> Nestle Careers applications are free and Nestle will never ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.nestlejobs.com/nestle-usa?page=1">Nestle Careers</a> (the official Nestle USA jobs pages: roles, pay ranges and requisition numbers); <a href="https://www.nestlejobs.com/nestle-usa?page=6">Nestle Careers</a> (further Nestle USA listings: warehouse and technician pay); <a href="https://jobs.auditfriendly.co/jobs/senior-compensation-analyst-nestle-30bbf553bc26">AuditFriendly Careers</a> (the Senior Compensation Analyst listing as published: salary, requisition number and sponsorship note).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the best paid Nestle USA role?</h3><p>The Senior Quality Manager Expert, remote, at $134,664.30 to $178,443 per annum.</p><h3>When do applications close?</h3><p>No closing date is given on the listings we've checked so the roles could close at any time once filled.</p><h3>How many jobs does Nestle USA have currently open?</h3><p>Glassdoor reported 389 open positions in the United States in November 2026.</p><h3>Does Nestle sponsor visas for these roles?</h3><p>The Senior Compensation Analyst post says it's not eligible for visa sponsorship; the other posts we've checked don't make any mention of sponsorship.</p>
$$,
