ed and no interview dates or start dates are provided. The listings don't state how many posts are available for each role. The only one of the roles in this lot to state its visa status is the Senior Compensation Analyst post is the only one in this roundup that states its visa position explicitly, so sponsorship for the others is not confirmed and would need to be checked directly with Nestle prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> Nestle Careers applications are free and Nestle will never ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.nestlejobs.com/nestle-usa?page=1">Nestle Careers</a> (the official Nestle USA jobs pages: roles, pay ranges and requisition numbers); <a href="https://www.nestlejobs.com/nestle-usa?page=6">Nestle Careers</a> (further Nestle USA listings: warehouse and technician pay); <a href="https://jobs.auditfriendly.co/jobs/senior-compensation-analyst-nestle-30bbf553bc26">AuditFriendly Careers</a> (the Senior Compensation Analyst listing as published: salary, requisition number and sponsorship note).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the best paid Nestle USA role?</h3><p>The Senior Quality Manager Expert, remote, at $134,664.30 to $178,443 per annum.</p><h3>When do applications close?</h3><p>No closing date is given on the listings we've checked so the roles could close at any time once filled.</p><h3>How many jobs does Nestle USA have currently open?</h3><p>Glassdoor reported 389 open positions in the United States in November 2026.</p><h3>Does Nestle sponsor visas for these roles?</h3><p>The Senior Compensation Analyst post says it's not eligible for visa sponsorship; the other posts we've checked don't make any mention of sponsorship.</p>
