ate on any of the listings we've checked, no interview dates or start dates are given and there's no indication of how many posts there are for each role. Only the technical sales post explicitly states its sponsorship position, so international applicants should check the sponsorship line on each live listing before they apply.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> Samsung Careers applications are free and Samsung will never ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://donutapply.com/companies/samsungelectronics/">DonutApply</a> (Samsung Electronics open US jobs as counted from the employer's own site: 454 posts, pay medians and locations); <a href="https://yabot.jobs/jobs/us/engineering-traditional/2026-11-02/staff-engineer-process-integration-san-jose-ca-1325568a-316a-4672-a207-5d5e1133248b">Yabot Jobs</a> (the Samsung Semiconductor Staff Engineer listing as published: pay range and duties); <a href="https://growthroles.com/jobs/sec-sr-manager-technical-sales-ossnms-intelligent-ran-ric-0bed98916e89d564">GrowthRoles</a> (the Samsung Senior Manager, Technical Sales listing as published: pay range and sponsorship note).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>How many jobs does Samsung have open in the USA?</h3><p>454 open US posts as of 24th November 2026, 245 of which were new in the last 30 days.</p><h3>What's the highest paid Samsung role?</h3><p>The Staff Engineer posts in San Jose, at $163,000 to $253,000 a year.</p><h3>Where is Samsung currently hiring the most in the USA?</h3><p>Dallas, Austin and the San Francisco Bay Area, with 107 open posts in Dallas and 96 in Austin.</p><h3>Is there a cap on the number of Samsung jobs I can apply for?</h3><p>Yes. Each candidate is capped at 10 applications across all open roles within a 6 month period.</p>
$$,
