'Jobs in Seattle USA are open across Washington state government, with an Assistant Attorney General role paying up to $157,080 and closing 7 December 2026.',
$$<p>The Washington State government is hiring in Seattle with legal, investigative and court roles available across the city. Jobs in Seattle USA in this roundup pay between $71,089 and $157,080 per year. The earliest closing date is 7th December 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>State of Washington, Attorney General's Office and Court of Appeals</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Assistant Attorney General, AGO Investigator/Analyst, Case Manager, Traffic Safety Resource Prosecutor</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$71,089 to $157,080 a year, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Closing 7 December 2026 for the Attorney General and court roles; 8 December 2026 for the prosecutor role</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the State of Washington careers portal and GovernmentJobs</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Law degree for the attorney and prosecutor roles; bachelor's degree plus five years of investigations experience for the investigator role</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application and assessment; the Attorney General's Office may contact applicants for further steps</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in Seattle USA involve</h2><p> Assistant Attorney General in the Environmental Protection Division (the headline role) where you would initiate and run prosecutions of environmental crimes. AGO Investigator/Analyst in the Environmental Protection Division to find, document and analyse evidence to prove civil environmental violations, including claims under the Clean Water Act, Clean Air Act etc). Court of Appeals, Division I is looking for a Case Manager to run case processing in Seattle. The City Attorney's Office is seeking a Traffic Safety Resource Prosecutor to lead the work on impaired driving cases across the state. All four are full time and based in downtown Seattle (with flexible or hybrid work available for the state positions). For those looking at <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> more broadly, we also have a guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/amazon-warehouse-jobs-pay-shifts-roles-and-how-to-apply-20261031">Amazon warehouse jobs</a> which is another very large employer in Seattle and has a very different way of getting in.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>The Assistant Attorney General role is for a qualified attorney with a strong background in civil or criminal litigation; the posting is represented by the Association of Washington Assistant Attorneys General. The Investigator/Analyst needs a bachelor's degree and five years of experience conducting investigations, including the authority to independently plan and conduct investigations in civil or criminal cases. The Case Manager role suits a highly detail-oriented applicant with court or case-processing experience, and the Traffic Safety Resource Prosecutor is a civil service exempt role for an experienced prosecutor. The listings do not state any nationality restriction, but applicants must be authorised to work in the United States.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>Pay varies considerably by role. Assistant Attorney General is $83,856 to $157,080 per year and the Traffic Safety Resource Prosecutor is $104,713.20 to $140,146.56 per year ($50.15 to $67.12/hour). The AGO Investigator/Analyst is $76,608 to $102,996 per year and the Case Manager is $71,089 to $93,227 per year (this includes the 5% premium pay for those working in King County). All state positions have the full Washington state employee benefits package (health, retirement and paid leave).</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply online via the State of Washington careers site (search by role title) or via GovernmentJobs for the City of Seattle Prosecutor position. The Assistant Attorney General and Case Manager applications close 7th December 2026 and the Traffic Safety Resource Prosecutor closes at 4pm Pacific on the 8th December 2026. The AGO Investigator/Analyst listing has no closing date in the text that we checked so applicants should check the live listing prior to applying. Applications must clearly demonstrate the essential criteria with specific examples from relevant experience.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings don't state how many posts there are for each role and give no interview dates or start dates. The AGO Investigator/Analyst listing has no closing date in the version we checked. None of the listings so international applicants should check directly with the hiring agency prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> State of Washington and City of Seattle applications are free and no government agency will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.governmentjobs.com/jobs/5521909-0/ago-investigator-analyst-environmental-protection-division-seattle">GovernmentJobs</a> (AGO Investigator/Analyst listing: salary, duties and qualifications); <a href="https://www.theladders.com/job/assistant-attorney-general-environmental-protection-division-seattle-stateofwashington-seattle-wa_89763905?source=similar">The Ladders</a> (State of Washington Assistant Attorney General listing: salary and closing date); <a href="https://www.theladders.com/job/case-manager-court-of-appeals-div-i-stateofwashington-seattle-wa_89934947">The Ladders</a> (Court of Appeals Case Manager listing: salary and closing date).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the highest paid job in this Seattle roundup?</h3><p>The Assistant Attorney General in the Environmental Protection Division at $83,856 to $157,080 a year.</p><h3>When do applications close?</h3><p>On 7 December 2026 for the Assistant Attorney General and Case Manager roles, and on 8 December 2026 for the Traffic Safety Resource Prosecutor.</p><h3>Do these roles provide for hybrid working?</h3><p>Yes, the state roles list flexible or hybrid working, and the prosecutor role is listed as flexible or hybrid.</p><h3>Is visa sponsorship available?</h3><p>The listings do not say, so applicants should check directly with the hiring agency before applying.</p>
$$,
