we checked so applicants should check the live listing prior to applying. Applications must clearly demonstrate the essential criteria with specific examples from relevant experience.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings don't state how many posts there are for each role and give no interview dates or start dates. The AGO Investigator/Analyst listing has no closing date in the version we checked. None of the listings so international applicants should check directly with the hiring agency prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> State of Washington and City of Seattle applications are free and no government agency will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.governmentjobs.com/jobs/5521909-0/ago-investigator-analyst-environmental-protection-division-seattle">GovernmentJobs</a> (AGO Investigator/Analyst listing: salary, duties and qualifications); <a href="https://www.theladders.com/job/assistant-attorney-general-environmental-protection-division-seattle-stateofwashington-seattle-wa_89763905?source=similar">The Ladders</a> (State of Washington Assistant Attorney General listing: salary and closing date); <a href="https://www.theladders.com/job/case-manager-court-of-appeals-div-i-stateofwashington-seattle-wa_89934947">The Ladders</a> (Court of Appeals Case Manager listing: salary and closing date).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the highest paid job in this Seattle roundup?</h3><p>The Assistant Attorney General in the Environmental Protection Division at $83,856 to $157,080 a year.</p><h3>When do applications close?</h3><p>On 7 December 2026 for the Assistant Attorney General and Case Manager roles, and on 8 December 2026 for the Traffic Safety Resource Prosecutor.</p><h3>Do these roles provide for hybrid working?</h3><p>Yes, the state roles list flexible or hybrid working, and the prosecutor role is listed as flexible or hybrid.</p><h3>Is visa sponsorship available?</h3><p>The listings do not say, so applicants should check directly with the hiring agency before applying.</p>
