(gen_random_uuid(), 'jobs-in-us-embassy-20261125', 'usa', 'USA',
'Jobs in US Embassy: Roles Pay Up to $150,391',
'Jobs in US Embassy: Roles Pay Up to $150,391',
'Jobs in US embassy missions are open worldwide, including a Bogota coordinator post paying $102,409 to $150,391 and closing 8 December 2026.',
'Jobs in US embassy missions are open worldwide, including a Bogota coordinator post paying $102,409 to $150,391 and closing 8 December 2026.',
$$<p>US embassies and missions are recruiting locally employed staff and US citizen family members with posts available from Ankara to Bogota. Jobs in US embassy missions featured in this roundup are paid between $34,799 and $150,391 per annum and the earliest closing dates are 30 November and 2 December 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>US Department of State, US Missions in Ankara, Monrovia, Belmopan and Bogota</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Security Clerk, Project Management Specialist, Human Resources Specialist, Management Coordinator</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>USD $34,799 to $150,391 a year, depending on the post</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Closing 30 November to 8 December 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the State Department Electronic Recruitment Application system</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Relevant experience for each post; eligibility depends on the hiring path stated in the announcement</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application through ERA; some posts are open only to US citizen family members</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in US embassy missions involve</h2><p>Embassy jobs fall into two very different categories and that distinction is important before you even start applying. There are the distinction matters before anyone applies. Locally employed staff posts (e.g. the Project Management Specialist in Monrovia and the Human Resources Specialist in Belmopan) which are filled locally and paid on a local scale with benefits (which may include health and separation pay). The Monrovia specialist manages foreign assistance finance and budgeting of State Department programmes, including the creation, execution and audit of the budget. The other group of posts are open only to US Citizen Eligible Family Members (e.g. the Security Clerk in Ankara who works in the Regional Security Office under Overseas Buildings Operations). The Bogota post is a different again: a personal services contract for a Management Coordinator who manages approximately 80 contract staff and a $75m annual budget for the Bureau of International Narcotics and Law Enforcement Affairs. Anyone considering work abroad can of course also take a look at our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/japan-work-visa-ssw-specified-skilled-worker-indians-20261120">Japan work visas</a> and our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> hub for other American employer routes.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>Eligibility is set post by post, and it is the first thing to check. The Monrovia and Belmopan posts are open to all interested applicants, including locally employed staff, household members, and third-country nationals. The Ankara Security Clerk is open only to US Citizen Eligible Family Members, and the Bogota coordinator post is open only to US citizens. The Dakar Safety Program Coordinator post, which paid XOF CFA16,191,877 a year, closed on 23 November 2026 and is therefore not counted as open here. Locally employed staff receive a compensation package that may include health, separation and other benefits, depending on the mission.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>Pay is by grade and location not by one scale. The Bogota Management Coordinator is FS-02 ($102,409 to $150,391) which is equivalent to GS-14. The Monrovia Project Management Specialist earns USD $41,536 per year at grade LE-1550 10, and the Ankara Security Clerk earns USD $34,799 per year at FP-9. The Belmopan Human Resources Specialist notes that no salary was listed in the announcement. The Dakar post had its pay quoted in West African CFA francs which shows how local the scales are. The Bogota contract is for twelve months from award with four optional one year extensions.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply via the Electronic Recruitment Application system at erajobs.state.gov, selecting the appropriate announcement number for the post. The Belmopan Human Resources Specialist closes on 30 November 2026 and the Ankara and Monrovia posts close on 2 December 2026. The Bogota Coordinator application must be emailed to the INL Personal Services Contract Team by 3pm ET on 8 December 2026. Each announcement has its own contact email address for questions and applicants should apply via the method specified in the announcement.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>Several announcements state no salary at all, including the Belmopan Human Resources Specialist post. None of the announcements in this roundup give interview dates or start dates. The announcements do not state whether locally employed posts carry visa sponsorship, and several are explicitly limited to US citizen family members or to local applicants, so readers should check the hiring path on each announcement before applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> State Department applications via ERA are free and no US mission will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://erajobs.state.gov/dos-era/vacancy/viewVacancyDetail.hms?_ref=t1bpwkrnpt0&amp;returnToSearch=true&amp;jnum=79058&amp;orgId=146">Electronic Recruitment Application</a> (the Embassy Ankara Security Clerk announcement: salary, dates and eligibility); <a href="https://erajobs.state.gov/dos-era/vacancy/viewVacancyDetail.hms?_ref=stqyefbbpt0&amp;returnToSearch=true&amp;jnum=79237&amp;orgId=82">Electronic Recruitment Application</a> (the Embassy Monrovia Project Management Specialist announcement: salary and dates); <a href="https://erajobs.state.gov/dos-era/vacancy/viewVacancyDetail.hms?_ref=nvdywxbbpt0&amp;returnToSearch=true&amp;jnum=79145&amp;orgId=161">Electronic Recruitment Application</a> (the Embassy Belmopan Human Resources Specialist announcement: dates and duties).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Can anyone apply for US embassy jobs?</h3><p>No, some posts are open to all applicants of interest. Others are open only to US Citizen Eligible Family Members or to US citizens only so you do need to check the hiring path on each announcement.</p><h3>What's the best paid job in the embassy?</h3><p>The Management Coordinator in Bogota at $102,409 to $150,391 per annum on a personal services contract.</p><h3>When do applications close?</h3><p> 30 November 2026 for Belmopan, 2 December for Ankara and Monrovia and 8 December for Bogota.</p><h3>Where do I apply?</h3><p>Via the State Department Electronic Recruitment Application system, apart from Bogota which is applied for by email.</p>
$$,
$$<p>US embassies and missions are recruiting locally employed staff and US citizen family members with posts available from Ankara to Bogota. Jobs in US embassy missions featured in this roundup are paid between $34,799 and $150,391 per annum and the earliest closing dates are 30 November and 2 December 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>US Department of State, US Missions in Ankara, Monrovia, Belmopan and Bogota</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Security Clerk, Project Management Specialist, Human Resources Specialist, Management Coordinator</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>USD $34,799 to $150,391 a year, depending on the post</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Closing 30 November to 8 December 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the State Department Electronic Recruitment Application system</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Relevant experience for each post; eligibility depends on the hiring path stated in the announcement</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application through ERA; some posts are open only to US citizen family members</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in US embassy missions involve</h2><p>Embassy jobs fall into two very different categories and that distinction is important before you even start applying. There are the distinction matters before anyone applies. Locally employed staff posts (e.g. the Project Management Specialist in Monrovia and the Human Resources Specialist in Belmopan) which are filled locally and paid on a local scale with benefits (which may include health and separation pay). The Monrovia specialist manages foreign assistance finance and budgeting of State Department programmes, including the creation, execution and audit of the budget. The other group of posts are open only to US Citizen Eligible Family Members (e.g. the Security Clerk in Ankara who works in the Regional Security Office under Overseas Buildings Operations). The Bogota post is a different again: a persona