mber 2026 and the Ankara and Monrovia posts close on 2 December 2026. The Bogota Coordinator application must be emailed to the INL Personal Services Contract Team by 3pm ET on 8 December 2026. Each announcement has its own contact email address for questions and applicants should apply via the method specified in the announcement.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>Several announcements state no salary at all, including the Belmopan Human Resources Specialist post. None of the announcements in this roundup give interview dates or start dates. The announcements do not state whether locally employed posts carry visa sponsorship, and several are explicitly limited to US citizen family members or to local applicants, so readers should check the hiring path on each announcement before applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> State Department applications via ERA are free and no US mission will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://erajobs.state.gov/dos-era/vacancy/viewVacancyDetail.hms?_ref=t1bpwkrnpt0&amp;returnToSearch=true&amp;jnum=79058&amp;orgId=146">Electronic Recruitment Application</a> (the Embassy Ankara Security Clerk announcement: salary, dates and eligibility); <a href="https://erajobs.state.gov/dos-era/vacancy/viewVacancyDetail.hms?_ref=stqyefbbpt0&amp;returnToSearch=true&amp;jnum=79237&amp;orgId=82">Electronic Recruitment Application</a> (the Embassy Monrovia Project Management Specialist announcement: salary and dates); <a href="https://erajobs.state.gov/dos-era/vacancy/viewVacancyDetail.hms?_ref=nvdywxbbpt0&amp;returnToSearch=true&amp;jnum=79145&amp;orgId=161">Electronic Recruitment Application</a> (the Embassy Belmopan Human Resources Specialist announcement: dates and duties).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Can anyone apply for US embassy jobs?</h3><p>No, some posts are open to all applicants of interest. Others are open only to US Citizen Eligible Family Members or to US citizens only so you do need to check the hiring path on each announcement.</p><h3>What's the best paid job in the embassy?</h3><p>The Management Coordinator in Bogota at $102,409 to $150,391 per annum on a personal services contract.</p><h3>When do applications close?</h3><p> 30 November 2026 for Belmopan, 2 December for Ankara and Monrovia and 8 December for Bogota.</p><h3>Where do I apply?</h3><p>Via the State Department Electronic Recruitment Application system, apart from Bogota which is applied for by email.</p>
