ARRAY['https://erajobs.state.gov/dos-era/vacancy/viewVacancyDetail.hms?_ref=t1bpwkrnpt0&returnToSearch=true&jnum=79058&orgId=146', 'https://erajobs.state.gov/dos-era/vacancy/viewVacancyDetail.hms?_ref=stqyefbbpt0&returnToSearch=true&jnum=79237&orgId=82', 'https://erajobs.state.gov/dos-era/vacancy/viewVacancyDetail.hms?_ref=nvdywxbbpt0&returnToSearch=true&jnum=79145&orgId=161'], NOW(), NOW(), NOW(), '2026-11-25'::timestamptz, NULL) ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

-- jobs-in-us-government-20261125 (usa; USA; verifiedAt 2026-11-25)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'jobs-in-us-government-20261125', 'usa', 'USA',
'Jobs in US Government: Federal Roles Close 30 November',
'Jobs in US Government: Federal Roles Close 30 November',
'Jobs in US government are open on USAJOBS, including Assistant US Attorney posts paying up to $197,100 and closing on 30 November 2026.',
'Jobs in US government are open on USAJOBS, including Assistant US Attorney posts paying up to $197,100 and closing on 30 November 2026.',
$$<p>Federal hiring is open across the US with DOJ attorney positions and defence health roles closing at the end of November. Jobs in US government in this round-up pay from $75,776 to $197,100 per year and the featured posts close on 30 November 2026.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>US Department of Justice, US Attorney's Offices; Defense Health Agency</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Assistant United States Attorney (Civil and Criminal); Management and Program Analyst</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$75,776 to $197,100 a year, depending on the role and locality pay</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Closing 30 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through USAJOBS</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Law degree and bar admission for the attorney posts; relevant federal experience for the analyst post</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application, interview and background checks; some posts are open only to current federal employees</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in US government involve</h2><p>An Assistant U.S. Attorney prosecutes or defends cases on behalf of the U.S. The Civil Division post in the Eastern District of Louisiana is a civil litigation post. The District of Maryland is hiring for both civil and criminal posts, covering work from civil claims to criminal prosecution. The Defense Health Agency post is a different kind of post: a Management and Program Analyst in the Financial Operations Directorate in Falls Church, VA and San Antonio, Texas, working on the finances behind military health care. Federal roles run on the General Schedule or administratively determined pay scales with locality pay on top for the more expensive areas. If you're looking at other <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs you</a> can also take a look at our report on the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/va-general-attorney-jobs-washington-dc-20261124">VA General Attorney jobs in Washington DC</a> which is another federal legal post with a fixed closing date.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>The attorney posts are open to qualified lawyers (law degree, bar admission and litigation experience) with pay being set in part by years of professional attorney experience. Assistant US Attorneys must reside in the district to which they are appointed or within 25 miles of it. The Defense Health Agency analyst post is narrower: it is open only to current competitive service federal employees, current federal employees eligible for career transition programmes, current excepted service employees and a very small number of other groups. It is not open to the general public. Federal hiring is generally restricted to US citizens and nationals and some of the positions are open to veterans, military spouses and people with disabilities.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>Assistant US Attorney pay is admin'd (administered) in part on years of experience and includes locality pay. The Louisiana post is $76,748-$197,100 (17.06% locality pay). The Maryland civil post pays $99,637 to $197,100, and the Maryland criminal post is $87,815-$197,100 (33.94% locality pay). The DHA analyst post is $75,776-$133,142 per year at grades 11-12 and salary negotiation may be available for those new to federal service. All federal employees get federal health coverage, retirement and paid leave.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply through USAJOBS, the federal government's official jobs site) by creating an account and submitting your full application package. The complete package must be submitted by 11.59pm ET on 30 November 2026. The Analyst post is also open until 30 November 2026. The full application package for the Attorney posts will comprise a cover letter, a resume (max two pages) and a writing sample. Recruitment incentives may be awarded for posts which are difficult to fill.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The attorney listings don't state how many posts are open in each district and provide no interview or start dates. The Defense Health Agency listing also doesn't state a post count. None of the listings in this round up state whether non-citizens can apply and as a general rule federal posts will require US citizenship so applicants should check the eligibility section of each USAJOBS announcement prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> USAJOBS applications are free and no federal agency will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.justice.gov/legal-careers/job/assistant-united-states-attorney-745">US Department of Justice</a> (Assistant US Attorney listing for Louisiana: salary, deadline and USAJOBS link); <a href="https://www.justice.gov/legal-careers/job/assistant-united-states-attorney-civil-248">US Department of Justice</a> (Assistant US Attorney Civil listing for Maryland: salary and deadline); <a href="https://www.usajobs.gov/job/891776700">USAJOBS</a> (the official federal jobs portal announcement).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>When do the federal applications close?</h3><p>On 30th November 2026 with the complete packages due by 11.59pm ET.</p><h3>What's the highest salary in this roundup?</h3><p>Up to $197,100 a year for the Assistant US Attorney posts (including locality pay).</p><h3>Can anyone apply for the Defense Health Agency analyst position?</h3><p>No, that announcement is open only to current federal employees and a very small number of other eligible groups, not to the general public.</p><h3>Where do I apply for Federal jobs?</h3><p>Through USAJOBS, the official federal jobs website) where each announcement has its own eligibility rules listed with it.</p>
$$,
