view or start dates. The Defense Health Agency listing also doesn't state a post count. None of the listings in this round up state whether non-citizens can apply and as a general rule federal posts will require US citizenship so applicants should check the eligibility section of each USAJOBS announcement prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> USAJOBS applications are free and no federal agency will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://www.justice.gov/legal-careers/job/assistant-united-states-attorney-745">US Department of Justice</a> (Assistant US Attorney listing for Louisiana: salary, deadline and USAJOBS link); <a href="https://www.justice.gov/legal-careers/job/assistant-united-states-attorney-civil-248">US Department of Justice</a> (Assistant US Attorney Civil listing for Maryland: salary and deadline); <a href="https://www.usajobs.gov/job/891776700">USAJOBS</a> (the official federal jobs portal announcement).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>When do the federal applications close?</h3><p>On 30th November 2026 with the complete packages due by 11.59pm ET.</p><h3>What's the highest salary in this roundup?</h3><p>Up to $197,100 a year for the Assistant US Attorney posts (including locality pay).</p><h3>Can anyone apply for the Defense Health Agency analyst position?</h3><p>No, that announcement is open only to current federal employees and a very small number of other eligible groups, not to the general public.</p><h3>Where do I apply for Federal jobs?</h3><p>Through USAJOBS, the official federal jobs website) where each announcement has its own eligibility rules listed with it.</p>
