-- jobs-in-usa-for-canadian-citizens-20261125 (usa; USA; verifiedAt 2026-11-25)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'jobs-in-usa-for-canadian-citizens-20261125', 'usa', 'USA',
'Jobs in USA for Canadian Citizens: TN Visa Nurse Roles',
'Jobs in USA for Canadian Citizens: TN Visa Nurse Roles',
'Jobs in USA for Canadian citizens include TN visa nursing roles paying $31 to $65 an hour, with relocation help and a path to a US nursing career.',
'Jobs in USA for Canadian citizens include TN visa nursing roles paying $31 to $65 an hour, with relocation help and a path to a US nursing career.',
$$<p>Canadian citizens can work in the US on a TN visa and nursing is by far the most straightforward route available at the moment with recruiters offering direct hire hospital positions. Jobs in USA for Canadian citizens in this list pay from $31 to $65/hour with sign-on bonuses and relocation help on some posts.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>IntelliStaff Medical and US hospital employers; TN Visa Guide board</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Emergency Department Registered Nurse, Dialysis Registered Nurse, Operating Room Registered Nurse</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$31 to $65 USD an hour, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Open now; one listing gives an apply-by date of 5 November 2027</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the recruiter or the TN visa job board</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Canadian citizenship, valid Canadian passport, active Canadian RN licence, NCLEX-RN passed</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application, interview and TN visa eligibility checks; VisaScreen certificate required</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in USA for Canadian citizens involve</h2><p>The TN visa (under the USMCA) allows qualified Canadian citizens to work in the US in one of the 63 designated professions without having to go through the H-1B lottery. Registered Nurse is one of those professions and is by far the most common. IntelliStaff Medical is actively recruiting experienced Canadian OR, CVOR and ED nurses for full time, permanent, direct hire positions with a US hospital employer. There's also a full time, permanent dialysis nurse position in Savannah, Georgia, offers a full-time, permanent role in a hospital based dialysis programme where the nurses will be rotating between the local clinics. The TN Visa Guide board has a number of TN posts listed for engineers, software developers and other USMCA professions. Those looking at other <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> can also take a look at our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/nursing-jobs-in-usa-for-foreign-nurses-nclex-visa-and-pay-guide-20261028">nursing jobs in the USA for foreign nurses</a> which goes into detail on the NCLEX, the visa and the pay.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>Applicants must be Canadian citizens with a valid Canadian passport, an active Canadian RN licence and a passed NCLEX-RN. The dialysis post requires a minimum of two years recent dialysis RN experience and the other posts require a minimum of 12 months recent inpatient hospital experience. A VisaScreen certificate is required and TN status can be granted for up to three years and is renewable (subject to eligibility). These are direct hire positions with the hospital employer (not agency), and the dialysis post. The TN route is only for Canadian and Mexican citizens, all other nationalities will use a different visa route.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The IntelliStaff emergency and operating room nurse posts pay $31 to $65 USD an hour, or about $64,480 to $135,200 a year at 40 hours a week, with sign-on bonuses and relocation assistance available. The Savannah dialysis post pays from $46 an hour, with a $10,000 USD sign-on bonus, up to $10,000 USD towards relocation and immigration, and employer-sponsored green card filing after 90 days of employment. Other Canadian nurse postings report $46 to $64 an hour with relocation packages. Pay varies with experience, specialty and location, and the postings quote US dollars, with Canadian-dollar equivalents given for guidance only.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply via the recruiter's listing or the TN visa job board. Start by speaking to a recruiter about the posts, pay, relocation support and the TN visa process. The IntelliStaff emergency nurse position was listed on the 5th November 2026 with an apply by date of the 5th November 2027. The dialysis post is a three-year commitment. Before you apply, make sure the duties and qualifications are in line with the USMCA Registered Nurse profession category (as advised by the TN Visa Guide board) and that you are VisaScreen and NCLEX ready.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings don't name the hospital employer and they don't give interview dates or start dates. The IntelliStaff listing has a very wide pay range which is not broken down by specialty or location. None of the listings. The TN route doesn't cover every occupation so applicants in any occupation other than nursing and the other 63 USMCA occupations should check that their occupation is covered prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> Applications via IntelliStaff Medical and the TN Visa Guide board are free. No real recruiter or employer will ever ask you to pay to apply, to have an interview or to take up a job.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://myrichmondhillontario.ca/jobs/emergency-department-registered-nurse-er-rn-usa-canadian-rns-4151250">IntelliStaff Medical</a> (the Emergency Department Registered Nurse listing for Canadian RNs: pay, TN eligibility and apply by date); <a href="https://tnvisaguide.ca/jobs">TN Visa Guide</a> (the TN visa job board: USMCA profession tagging and open TN roles); <a href="https://ca.indeed.com/q-lmia,-dialysis-nurse-l-ontario-jobs.html">Indeed Canada</a> (the Dialysis Registered Nurse listing for Canadian citizens: pay, sign-on bonus and TN support).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What is the TN visa?</h3><p>A work route under the USMCA for Canadian and Mexican citizens in one of the 63 listed professions (including Registered Nurse) for a period of up to three years and renewable.</p><h3>What do TN visa nurses earn in the USA?</h3><p>From $31 to $65 an hour in this round up (i.e. $64,480 to $135,200 a year at 40 hours per week) with sign on and relocation assistance on a number of the posts.</p><h3>Do I need the NCLEX to work as a nurse in the USA?</h3><p>Yes. The listings require a passed NCLEX-RN, an active Canadian RN licence and a VisaScreen certificate.</p><h3>Can Canadians apply for non-nursing TN jobs as well?</h3><p>Yes. The TN Visa Guide board has TN tagged posts for engineers, software developers and other USMCA professions, although nursing dominates the verified posts.</p>
$$,
$$<p>Canadian citizens can work in the US on a TN visa and nursing is by far the most straightforward route available at the moment with recruiters offering direct hire hospital positions. Jobs in USA for Canadian citizens in this list pay from $31 to $65/hour with sign-on bonuses and relocation help on some posts.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>IntelliStaff Medical and US hospital employers; TN Visa Guide board</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Emergency Department Registered Nurse, Dialysis Registered Nurse, Operating Room Registered Nurse</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$31 to $65 USD an hour, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Open now; one listing gives an apply-by date of 5 November 2027</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the recruiter or the TN visa job board</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Canadian citizenship, valid Canadian passport, active Canadian RN licence, NCLEX-RN passed</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application, interview and TN visa eligibility checks; VisaScreen certificate required</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What jobs in USA for Canadian citizens involve</h2><p>The TN visa (under the USMCA) allows qualified Canadian citizens to work in the US in one of the 63 designated professions without having to go through the H-1B lottery. Registered Nurse is one of those professions and is by far the most common. IntelliStaff Medical is actively recruiting experienced Canadian OR, CVOR and ED nurses for full time, permanent, direct hire positions with a US hospital employer. There's also a full time, permanent dialysis nurse position in Savannah, Georgia, offers a full-time, permanent role in a hospital based dialysis programme where the nurses will be rotating between the local clinics. The TN Visa Guide board has a number of TN posts listed for engineers, software developers and other USMCA professions. Those looking at other <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> can also take a look at our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/nursing-jobs-in-usa-for-foreign-nurses-nclex-visa-and-pay-guide-20261028">nursing jobs in the USA for foreign nurses</a> which goes into detail on the NCLEX, the visa and the pay.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>Applicants must be Canadian citizens with a valid Canadian passport, an active Canadian RN licence and a passed NCLEX-RN. The dialysis post requires a minimum of two years recent dialysis RN experience and the other posts require a minimum of 12 months recent inpatient hospital experience. A VisaScreen certificate is required and TN status can be granted for up to three years and is renewable (subject to eligibility). These are direct hire positions with the hospital employer (not agency), and the dialysis post. The TN route is only for Canadian and Mexican citizens, all other nationalities will use a different visa route.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The IntelliStaff emergency and operating room nurse posts pay $31 to $65 USD an hour, or about $64,480 to $135,200 a year at 40 hours a week, with sign-on bonuses and relocation assistance available. The Savannah dialysis post pays from $46 an hour, with a $10,000 USD sign-on bonus, up to $10,000 USD towards relocation and immigration, and employer-sponsored green card filing after 90 days of employment. Other Canadian nurse postings report $46 to $64 an hour with relocation packages. Pay varies with experience, specialty and location, and the postings quote US dollars, with Canadian-dollar equivalents given for guidance only.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply via the recruiter's listing or the TN visa job board. Start by speaking to a recruiter about the posts, pay, relocation support and the TN visa process. The IntelliStaff emergency nurse position was listed on the 5th November 2026 with an apply by date of the 5th November 2027. The dialysis post is a three-year commitment. Before you apply, make sure the duties and qualifications are in line with the USMCA Registered Nurse profession category (as advised by the TN Visa Guide board) and that you are VisaScreen and NCLEX ready.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>The listings don't name the hospital employer and they don't give interview dates or start dates. The IntelliStaff listing has a very wide pay range which is not broken down by specialty or location. None of the listings. The TN route doesn't cover every occupation so applicants in any occupation other than nursing and the other 63 USMCA occupations should check that their occupation is covered prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> Applications via IntelliStaff Medical and the TN Visa Guide board are free. No real recruiter or employer will ever ask you to pay to apply, to have an interview or to take up a job.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://myrichmondhillontario.ca/jobs/emergency-department-registered-nurse-er-rn-usa-canadian-rns-4151250">IntelliStaff Medical</a> (the Emergency Department Registered Nurse listing for Canadian RNs: pay, TN eligibility and apply by date); <a href="https://tnvisaguide.ca/jobs">TN Visa Guide</a> (the TN visa job board: USMCA profession tagging and open TN roles); <a href="https://ca.indeed.com/q-lmia,-dialysis-nurse-l-ontario-jobs.html">Indeed Canada</a> (the Dialysis Registered Nurse listing for Canadian citizens: pay, sign-on bonus and TN support).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What is the TN visa?</h3><p>A work route under the USMCA for Canadian and Mexican citizens in one of the 63 listed professions (including Registered Nurse) for a period of up to three years and renewable.</p><h3>What do TN visa nurses earn in the USA?</h3><p>From $31 to $65 an hour in this round up (i.e. $64,480 to $135,200 a year at 40 hours per week) with sign on and relocation assistance on a number of the posts.</p><h3>Do I need the NCLEX to work as a nurse in the USA?</h3><p>Yes. The listings require a passed NCLEX-RN, an active Canadian RN licence and a VisaScreen certificate.</p><h3>Can Canadians apply for non-nursing TN jobs as well?</h3><p>Yes. The TN Visa Guide board has TN tagged posts for engineers, software developers and other USMCA professions, although nursing dominates the verified posts.</p>
$$,
