-- remote-jobs-japanese-20261125 (remote; Japan; verifiedAt 2026-11-25)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'remote-jobs-japanese-20261125', 'remote', 'Japan',
'Remote Jobs Japanese: Language Roles Pay Up to $100/hr',
'Remote Jobs Japanese: Language Roles Pay Up to $100/hr',
'Remote jobs Japanese speakers can apply for now include a $100-an-hour AI training role at Begun and Mercor linguistic posts at $40 to $50 an hour.',
'Remote jobs Japanese speakers can apply for now include a $100-an-hour AI training role at Begun and Mercor linguistic posts at $40 to $50 an hour.',
$$<p>Remote jobs Japanese speakers can find are very much in the AI training space, with platforms paying native and fluent speakers to evaluate, translate and record the Japanese language work. Remote work for Japanese speakers is currently paying from $30 to $100 an hour (mostly on a part time or contract terms.</p><table><tbody><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>Begun (formerly Ethos), Mercor, micro1, Welocalize</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Japanese Language and Cultural Fluency Consultant, Japanese Linguistic Expert, Bilingual Japanese Language Specialist</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$30 to $100 an hour, depending on the role</td></tr><tr><td>Application dates</td><td>Open now; no fixed closing date stated</td></tr><tr><td>Application route</td><td>Online through the hiring platform</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Native or near-native Japanese; 4 or more years of translation or localisation experience for the top-paid role</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Application and assessment; language level is tested</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>What remote jobs Japanese speakers do</h2><p>The work is AI training: creating, evaluating and refining AI-generated documents, spreadsheets and slide decks in both Japanese and English. Accuracy, tone and cultural appropriateness are all checked. The Begun consultant role is at $100/hr and is for bilinguals who can review high value business and legal content, perform localisation and tone adaptation checks and assess cultural context and etiquette. Mercor's Japanese Linguistic Experts are working on an AI research project with a major research lab and their Bilingual Japanese Language Specialist is writing expert level prompts in Japanese on a range of sensitive topics as part of their AI safety work. Welocalize have a number of short coding evaluation projects on offer (e.g. a Japanese speaking Rust specialist at $75-$90/hr for a one week project). A tracker found 62 Japanese AI training jobs open as of 24th November 2026 across 14 platforms, Mercor being the biggest employer. Those looking for other <a href="https://growentix.cloud/remote">remote work options</a> can also check out our guide to <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/remote-customer-service-jobs-no-experience-what-employers-actually-want-20261019">remote customer service jobs with no experience</a> as a different route into remote work.</p><h2>Who can apply</h2><p>These roles require native or near-native Japanese, with a strong command of grammar, syntax, and style, plus clear communication in English. The Begun consultant role needs four or more years of professional translation or cross-cultural business experience. The Mercor specialist role is based in Japan or the wider East Asia region, while the Mercor linguistic experts and the micro1 bilingual expert are listed as worldwide remote. The Welocalize coding roles are remote in Japan and need programming skills alongside Japanese. Most roles are part-time or contract, with flexible hours rather than a fixed weekly schedule.</p><h2>What it pays</h2><p>The Begun consultant is $100/hr for 5 to 20 hours a week, or up to $2,000 a week at the top end). Welocalize pay is $75-$90/hr for their coding evaluation work. The micro1 bilingual expert pays $30 to $65 an hour, the Mercor linguists are $50/hr and the Mercor bilingual specialist is $48-$52/hr. Of the 62 open Japanese AI training jobs tracked on 24th November 2026, most are in the $26-$65/hr range with a typical rate of $40/hr (based on 49 of the posted rates). Again these are contract rates, not salaries and hours are not guaranteed.</p><h2>How to apply</h2><p>Apply via the platform that has the role (Begun, Mercor, micro1 or Welocalize) by creating an account and then completing the application and language test. The Begun role was listed on 2 November 2026 and was still open on 24 November. The Mercor role for linguistic experts was listed on 30 October 2026. There's no stated closing date on any of the roles we looked at so they will close when filled. You'll need to demonstrate native Japanese and the requisite translation/localisation/technical experience for the role.</p><h2>What the notice does not say</h2><p>There's no closing date on any of the listings that we've checked and for the majority of the roles there's no guaranteed weekly hour count is guaranteed for most roles. The listings don't state how many posts there are for each role and they don't state whether the work would lead to a longer term position. None of the listings state that it's a visa position as it's remote and contract work so applicants should check the location restriction on each listing prior to applying.</p><p><strong>Never pay anyone to apply for this job.</strong> All applications to Begun, Mercor, micro1 and Welocalize are free and no real platform will ever ask you to pay anything for an application, an assessment or a job offer.</p><p>Sources: <a href="https://aitrainer.jobs/jobs/120024-japanese-language-cultural-fluency-consultant-ethos">AI Trainer Jobs</a> (the Begun Japanese Language and Cultural Fluency Consultant listing: pay, hours and duties); <a href="https://hiring.sojistudio.com/jobs/japanese-linguistic-experts">SOJI Studio</a> (the Mercor Japanese Linguistic Experts listing: pay, location and requirements); <a href="https://remotive.com/remote/jobs/all-others/bilingual-japanese-language-specialist-6488421">Remotive</a> (the Mercor Bilingual Japanese Language Specialist listing: pay, location and duties).</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What's the highest paid remote Japanese role?</h3><p>The Japanese Language and Cultural Fluency Consultant at Begun, $100 an hour for 5 to 20 hours per week.</p><h3>Do I need to be a native Japanese speaker?</h3><p>Yes. The roles are looking for native or near-native Japanese with a very strong command of grammar, syntax and style.</p><h3>Are these full-time jobs?</h3><p>No, most are part time/contract roles with flexible hours rather than fixed full time positions.</p><h3>Can I apply from anywhere in the world?</h3><p>Some roles are fully remote worldwide, others are restricted to Japan or East Asia so be sure to check the location restrictions on each listing.</p>
$$,
