VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'bitcoin-price-below-60000-20261125', 'news', 'Global',
'Bitcoin price falls below $60,000 as tariff fears hit markets',
'Bitcoin price falls below $60,000 as tariff fears hit markets',
'The Bitcoin price fell below $60,000 on Tuesday, down nearly 8% from Monday''s high, as reports of new US tariffs rattled risk assets.',
'The Bitcoin price fell below $60,000 on Tuesday, down nearly 8% from Monday''s high, as reports of new US tariffs rattled risk assets.',
$$<p> Bitcoin prices dropped below $60,000 on Tuesday 24th November 2026 as news of new US tariffs sent markets into a tailspin and completely wiped out the very short-lived rally that had followed Nvidia's board reinstating Jensen Huang.</p>

<table>
<tr><td>Event</td><td>Bitcoin falls below $60,000</td></tr>
<tr><td>Date</td><td>24 November 2026, US trading session</td></tr>
<tr><td>Price</td><td>Below $59,500 at the session low</td></tr>
<tr><td>Fall from Monday high</td><td>Nearly 8% from $64,500</td></tr>
<tr><td>Fall over one month</td><td>About 25%</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What happened</h2>

<p>Bitcoin fell below $59,500 on Bitstamp during Tuesday's US trading session, down about 2.2% on the day and nearly 8% from Monday's $64,500 high, <a href="https://www.cwbsc.com/news/bitcoin-slides-amid-us-tariff-nerves-as-anthropic-falls-belo-BggzjoM3">Cointelegraph</a> reported. <a href="https://www.coindesk.com/tech/2026/11/24/live-updates-bitcoin-pulls-back-to-usd60-000-as-stock-rally-fails-to-budge-crypto">CoinDesk</a> reported Bitcoin at $59,576.97 in its live coverage, down 5.8% over 24 hours and down 25% over the past month, trading about 15% below its 200-day moving average just above $71,000. <a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/china/global-markets-global-markets-2026-11-25/">Reuters</a> reported Bitcoin at $59,257.71, down 1%, while ether slid 1.1% to $1,660.52.</p>

<p>The trigger was trade. The Wall Street Journal reported that US Trade Representative Jamieson Greer could announce the results of an investigation into foreign industrial subsidies as soon as this week, with partners such as the EU, Japan and South Korea potentially facing levies of up to 15%. US equities opened lower on the news, with the S and P 500 down 0.7% and the Nasdaq Composite 2% lower, and Bitcoin fell with them. Risk assets have stayed highly sensitive to tariff headlines since President Donald Trump first unveiled sweeping tariffs in April 2025, and the Supreme Court struck down tariffs imposed under emergency economic powers in February 2026.</p>

<h2>What the Bitcoin price fall means for jobs</h2>

<p>A 25% monthly drop in Bitcoin isn't just a trader's issue. The crypto companies that were all over the place during the boom have been cutting people on a regular basis as prices have come down and the wider chill has spread to the exchanges, the blockchain developers and the VC funding. The most immediate signal is of course confidence. When Bitcoin and the tech stocks go down together on the same headline, it tells the entire tech sector that the market is still quite fragile and that hiring plans are going to stay on hold. The level to watch is $58,500 (the June low) as a close below that could trigger a fall towards Bitcoin's realised price of $53,200. Growentix tracks the market mood via our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-stock-selloff-sp-500-correction-20261124">AI selloff coverage</a> and the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles">News hub</a> which tracks how market moves impact hiring.</p>

<h2>What the sources do not say</h2>

<p>The sources do not agree on the exact low: Cointelegraph put it below $59,500 on Bitstamp, CoinDesk reported an overnight low of $59,400, and Reuters quoted $59,257.71 in Asian trading, so the precise figure depends on the exchange and the time. The sources also do not say whether the tariff announcement will actually come this week, only that it could, and they do not establish that tariffs caused the whole fall — the Nvidia-driven rally was already fading, and Anthropic shares were falling at the same time.</p>

<p>Sources: <a href="https://www.coindesk.com/tech/2026/11/24/live-updates-bitcoin-pulls-back-to-usd60-000-as-stock-rally-fails-to-budge-crypto">CoinDesk</a> for the live prices and the $58,500 level; <a href="https://www.cwbsc.com/news/bitcoin-slides-amid-us-tariff-nerves-as-anthropic-falls-belo-BggzjoM3">Cointelegraph</a> for the session low and the tariff trigger; <a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/china/global-markets-global-markets-2026-11-25/">Reuters</a> for the Asian market prices and Ether.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>How far has Bitcoin dropped this month?</h3>
<p>About 25% over the past month, from Monday's high of about $64,500 to below $59,500 on Tuesday.</p>
<h3>Why did Bitcoin go down on Tuesday?</h3>
<p>Reports that the Trump administration could be announcing new tariff increases as early as this week have hit risk assets with US equities and crypto both in freefall.</p>
