-- deere-earnings-q4-preview-20261125 (news; USA; verifiedAt NULL)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt", "verifiedAt", "authorName")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'deere-earnings-q4-preview-20261125', 'news', 'USA',
'Deere earnings due as farm slump tests tractor maker',
'Deere earnings due as farm slump tests tractor maker',
'Deere earnings land on Wednesday, with analysts expecting about $4.07 a share as weak farm spending and tariff costs squeeze the tractor maker.',
'Deere earnings land on Wednesday, with analysts expecting about $4.07 a share as weak farm spending and tariff costs squeeze the tractor maker.',
$$<p>Deere earnings are out Wednesday 25th November 2026 (before the US market opens) with the company providing its first fiscal 2027 outlook. It's a year of weak farm spend and increasing tariff costs.</p>

<table>
<tr><td>Event</td><td>Deere fiscal Q4 2026 results</td></tr>
<tr><td>Release</td><td>25 November 2026, before the market opens</td></tr>
<tr><td>EPS estimate</td><td>About $4.03 to $4.07 a share</td></tr>
<tr><td>Revenue estimate</td><td>About $10.3 billion to $10.4 billion</td></tr>
<tr><td>Key question</td><td>First fiscal 2027 outlook</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What to expect on Wednesday</h2>

<p>Wall Street is looking for Deere to report net income of around $1.1bn (about flat year on year), according to <a href="https://www.barrons.com/articles/deere-earnings-stock-price-8ce3b9df">Barron's</a>, with a consensus of around $4.07 a share and revenue of c.$10.3bn. <a href="https://www.tradingview.com/news/tradingview:9e0c0806bcf04:0-de-q4-26-earnings-eps-estimate-is-4-03-usd/">TradingView</a> has the estimate slightly lower at $4.03 a share on $10.38bn revenue. In the prior quarter Deere earned $5.10 a share on revenue of $11.00 billion, beating expectations. Deere shares have been up 32% in 2026 but were down 3.04% on Tuesday at $613.76 as investors awaited the numbers.</p>

<p>The view is more important than the quarter. Deere is due to provide its first fiscal 2027 outlook with Wall Street expecting net income of around $5.9bn (up from $4.9bn in 2026). <a href="https://stockrow.com/DE/news">Stockrow</a> says Deere expects North American large agricultural equipment sales to be down 15-20% in fiscal 2026 and tariffs could cost the company nearly $1bn in fiscal 2027. Shares trade at around 29x forward earnings, well above the five-year average of around 20x, so the outlook will be a key test of whether the recovery that investors are already pricing in is supported.</p>

<h2>What Deere earnings mean for jobs</h2>

<p>Deere is the bellwether for rural America in that when farmers stop buying tractors, the effect is felt first in the dealerships, the parts suppliers and the factory towns. Weak farm spend and low commodity prices have already pulled the shares down prior to the report and a very cautious 2027 outlook would be consistent with continued softness in farm equipment hiring into next year. The tariff cost is the other jobs signal (nearly $1bn in extra cost in fiscal 2027 is money that can't go to wages or investment). On the flip side a full year profit of $5.9bn would suggest the company still expects a recovery and precision agriculture remains the growth area within the business. Growentix tracks US industrial hiring via our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-stock-selloff-sp-500-correction-20261124">market coverage</a> and the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/usa">USA jobs</a> hub.</p>

<h2>What the sources do not say</h2>

<p>No one can say what Deere will actually report. The estimates vary from $4.03 to $4.17 a share and revenue from $10.3 billion to $10.68 billion depending on the source. No one can say what the 2027 outlook will be (that's the number the market is waiting for). There's no comment on whether they will be cutting factory jobs or adding them, or how the tariff costs will be split between price and margin.</p>

<p>Sources: <a href="https://www.barrons.com/articles/deere-earnings-stock-price-8ce3b9df">Barron's</a> for the earnings expectations and the 2027 outlook; <a href="https://www.tradingview.com/news/tradingview:9e0c0806bcf04:0-de-q4-26-earnings-eps-estimate-is-4-03-usd/">TradingView</a> for the $4.03 estimate and the earnings history; <a href="https://stockrow.com/DE/news">Stockrow</a> for the sales outlook and tariff costs.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>When does Deere report their earnings?</h3>
<p>Deere reports its fiscal fourth-quarter 2026 results on Wednesday 25th November 2026, before the market opens.</p>
<h3>What do the analysts think Deere is going to do?</h3>
<p>Analysts expect earnings of around $4.03 to $4.07 a share on revenue of about $10.3 billion, with the first fiscal 2027 outlook being the key figure.</p>
