(gen_random_uuid(), 'ella-langley-choosin-texas-ties-drake-hot-100-record-20261125', 'pop-music', 'USA',
'Ella Langley Choosin Texas Ties Drake Hot 100 Record',
'Ella Langley Choosin Texas Ties Drake Hot 100 Record',
'Ella Langley Choosin Texas spends a 29th week at No. 1 on the Hot 100, tying Drake''s record for the most weeks at the top in a single calendar year.',
'Ella Langley Choosin Texas spends a 29th week at No. 1 on the Hot 100, tying Drake''s record for the most weeks at the top in a single calendar year.',
$$<p>Ella Langley Choosin Texas has spent a 29th week at No.1 on the Billboard Hot 100, equalling Drake's record for most weeks at the top of the chart by a single artist in a single calendar year. The song topped the Hot 100 dated 28th November 2026 (announced 23rd November) and is now the longest running No.1 of all time by a huge margin.</p>

<table>
<tr><td>Song</td><td>"Choosin' Texas" — Ella Langley</td></tr>
<tr><td>Album</td><td><em>Dandelion</em> (released 17 October 2025)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Billboard Hot 100</td><td>No. 1 for a 29th week (chart dated 28 November 2026); 57 weeks on chart</td></tr>
<tr><td>Latest week</td><td>16.9 million US streams, 45.5 million radio audience, 6,000 sales (up 68%)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Calendar-year record</td><td>Ties Drake's 29 weeks at No. 1 in 2018</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hot Country Songs</td><td>No. 1 for a 50th week, tying "Meant to Be"</td></tr>
<tr><td>Streaming Songs</td><td>No. 1 for a 28th week</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What happened</h2>

<p>"Choosin' Texas" first hit No. 1 in February 2026 and has barely budged from the top since, with only a three week stint from Taylor Swift's "Patient Zero" in October to break it. It broke the all time Hot 100 longevity record in September when its 23rd week at No. 1 surpassed the 22 weeks that Mariah Carey's "All I Want for Christmas Is You" had previously held. The latest chart week comes in the days after Langley's historic night at the 60th CMA Awards on 18th November (where she took home six of nine awards, including Entertainer of the Year, Female Vocalist of the Year and Album of the Year for <em>Dandelion</em>) and two days after she received seven Grammy nominations. According to Luminate data as cited by <a href="https://www.whiskeyriff.com/2026/11/23/ella-langley-is-closing-in-on-even-more-history-as-choosin-texas-spends-its-29th-week-at-1-on-the-hot-100/">Whiskey Riff</a>, the song had 16.9 million official US streams and a 45.5 million radio audience in the most recent tracking week. Sales also jumped 68% to 6,000 in the same week as a result of the awards and Grammy buzz. The <a href="https://growentix.cloud/popmusic">Pop Music</a> hub has the rest of the week's chart news and our report on her <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ella-langley-choosin-texas-28-weeks-hot-100-record-20261117">28th week at No. 1</a> covers the run up to that point.</p>

<h2>What the Ella Langley Choosin Texas record means</h2>

<p>The calendar year tie is the eye-catcher in terms of how it was achieved. Drake set the record in 2018 with three separate No. 1s (God's Plan for 11 weeks, In My Feelings for 10 and Nice for What for eight — while Langley has achieved the same total with a single country record (co-produced by Miranda Lambert) as <a href="https://www.martincid.com/music-en/ella-langley-choosin-texas-ties-drake-single-year-record/">Martin Cid Magazine</a> points out. Usher was the previous holder of the record with 28 weeks in 2004 (across four No. 1s). The run is also setting the country charts on fire with a 50th week atop Hot Country Songs which is the longest such reign in that chart's history (held previously by Florida Georgia Line and Bebe Rexha's Meant to Be) and the song has now spent 57 weeks on the Hot 100. "Choosin' Texas" was written with Lambert, Luke Dick and Joybeth Taylor and it's the first time a woman to top the Hot 100, Hot Country Songs and Country Airplay charts at the same time.</p>

<h2>What the sources do not say</h2>

<p>Nothing in the report states whether Langley will actually be performing at the Grammys (she has seven nominations) or whether "Choosin' Texas" will continue to hold the No. 1 spot for a 30th week (the next chart is the first one to reflect the full week of her CMA sales against the holiday spike which has already seen Mariah Carey into the top five. The sources have no view on that at all. The sources also don't break down the sales by format so we don't know how much of the 68% sales increase came from physical sales.</p>

<p>Sources: <a href="https://www.yahoo.com/entertainment/music/articles/ella-langley-choosin-texas-leads-175728348.html">Yahoo Entertainment (Billboard)</a>, <a href="https://www.whiskeyriff.com/2026/11/23/ella-langley-is-closing-in-on-even-more-history-as-choosin-texas-spends-its-29th-week-at-1-on-the-hot-100/">Whiskey Riff</a>, <a href="https://www.martincid.com/music-en/ella-langley-choosin-texas-ties-drake-single-year-record/">Martin Cid Magazine</a>, <a href="https://ratingsgamemusic.com/2026/11/23/top-5-singles-on-the-billboard-hot-100-this-week-11-23-ella-langley-stella-lefty-tame-impala/">RGM</a>.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>How many weeks has Choosin' Texas been at No.1 on the Hot 100?</h3>
<p>29 weeks on the chart as of the 28th November 2026 issue — the longest running No.1 in Hot 100 history.</p>
<h3>Whose record did Ella Langley match?</h3>
<p>Drake's record of 29 weeks at No.1 in a single calendar year (achieved in 2018 across three songs) was matched by Langley with one song. One more week at No.1 and she'd have the record.</p>
