$$<p>sombr My Body Isn't Ready has reached No.3 on the UK Singles Chart, becoming the American artist's biggest hit in the UK to date. The track, which came out in July, is up two places this week (20-26 November 2026) to overtake his previous UK hits 'undressed' and "Homewrecker" in the process.</p>

<table>
<tr><td>Song</td><td>"My Body Isn't Ready" — sombr</td></tr>
<tr><td>Released</td><td>July 2026</td></tr>
<tr><td>UK Singles Chart</td><td>No. 3 (chart week 20–26 November 2026), up from No. 5</td></tr>
<tr><td>Chart journey</td><td>Debuted at No. 27, reached the Top 10 in October</td></tr>
<tr><td>Previous best</td><td>"undressed" and "Homewrecker"</td></tr>
<tr><td>UK No. 1 this week</td><td>"Babydoll" — Jamie Miller (fifth week)</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What happened</h2>

<p>The climb has been very gradual really. <a href="https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/sombr-jamie-miller-justice-gta-6-number-1-singles-chart/">Official Charts Company</a> stats show it started at No.27, worked its way up, broke into the Top 10 in October and reached No.5 last week before moving up to No.3. That makes it sombr's highest charting UK single to date (above "undressed" and "Homewrecker". At the top of the same chart, Jamie Miller's "Babydoll" is at No.1 for a fifth week in a row. Justice, Tame Impala and SZA's "Flower in a Hurricane" leap from No.32 to No.9 thanks to the release of Grand Theft Auto VI (<a href="http://www.music-news.com/news/UK/192386/Justice-Tame-Impala-and-SZA-Storm-UK-Top-10-as-GTA-VI-sparks-massive-chart-surge">Music News</a>). Tate McRae's "Housewife" is at No.4 and Sienna Spiro's "Great Expectation" at No.5. The <a href="https://growentix.cloud/popmusic">Pop Music</a> hub has the rest of the week's chart news and our report on <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/james-blunt-airplane-mode-uk-number-one-20261124">James Blunt's UK No.1 album</a> covers the other side of this week's British charts.</p>

<h2>What the sombr My Body Isn't Ready climb means</h2>

<p>A song released in July which peaks in late November is the very antithesis of the normal chart story (new song comes in at the top and then tumbles). "My Body Isn't Ready" has been climbing almost every step of the way really from 27 on debut, into the Top 10 in October, to 5 last week and now 3. That's a classic case of sustained streaming growth rather than a single viral moment. That's significant as the top of the UK chart is about to be completely inundated with Christmas songs - Wham's "Last Christmas" is already at 12 and Mariah Carey's "All I Want for Christmas Is You" has jumped 18 places to 18. For a non-seasonal song to be peaking right now, just before the Christmas onslaught. The window is very narrow though with the Christmas No.1 race heating up and the next chart (out on Friday 27th November) going a long way to determine whether sombr can go any higher.</p>

<h2>What the sources do not say</h2>

<p>There's nothing in the report on the chart week's performance to give us any streaming or sales figures for "My Body Isn't Ready" as it has climbed to No.3. We don't know if sombr have any UK performances or TV appearances lined up to help the song move any further, nor do we know if a new single is on the way. The US performance of the track is not mentioned at all, only its position in the UK.</p>

<p>Sources: <a href="https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/sombr-jamie-miller-justice-gta-6-number-1-singles-chart/">Official Charts Company</a>, <a href="http://www.music-news.com/news/UK/192386/Justice-Tame-Impala-and-SZA-Storm-UK-Top-10-as-GTA-VI-sparks-massive-chart-surge">Music News</a>, <a href="https://energyradio.uk/uk-charts-this-week-jamie-miller-five-weeks-number-1-20-november-2026/">Energy Radio</a>.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>What's Sombr's highest charting UK single?</h3>
<p>'My Body Isn't Ready' is at No.3 on the Official Singles Chart for the week of 20-26th November 2026, overtaking his previous two hits 'undressed' and 'homewrecker'.</p>
