'Taylor Swift Brenda Lee surprise in Nashville saw the pop star present the 81-year-old legend with a Diamond plaque for Rockin Around the Christmas Tree.',
$$<p>The Taylor Swift Brenda Lee visit in Nashville was the warmest moment of the Christmas season. She turned up to present the 81-year-old with a Diamond plaque for 'Rockin' Around the Christmas Tree'. The visit happened on 16th November and Lee posted a video of it on social media on 23rd November.</p>

<table>
<tr><td>Song</td><td>"Rockin' Around the Christmas Tree" — Brenda Lee</td></tr>
<tr><td>Recorded</td><td>1958, when Lee was 13 years old</td></tr>
<tr><td>Certification</td><td>RIAA Diamond — more than 10 million units in the US</td></tr>
<tr><td>Surprise visit</td><td>16 November 2026, Nashville; video shared 23 November</td></tr>
<tr><td>Milestone</td><td>Only the second Christmas song ever to go Diamond</td></tr>
<tr><td>Songwriter / producer</td><td>Johnny Marks / Owen Bradley</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What happened</h2>

<p>The video opens with Swift entering a room holding the diamond plaque, and Lee jokingly asking if the pop superstar has grown a "foot" since they last saw each other, according to <a href="https://people.com/brenda-lee-gets-emotional-taylor-swift-presents-diamond-plaque-rockin-around-the-christmas-tree-12274708">People</a>. "I'm one of the many, many fans of your iconic song 'Rockin' Around the Christmas Tree'," Swift tells her. "You recorded this when you were only 13 years old, and it is one of only two Christmas songs to ever reach this milestone. You're in very good company with Mariah Carey all the way at the top, and this is yours now, and it'll be yours forever." Lee tears up as she speaks about the song's writer, Johnny Marks, who died in 1985, and producer Owen Bradley, who died in 1998. "It means the world to me that 'Rockin' Around The Christmas Tree' is Diamond," Lee said in a statement carried by <a href="https://www.universalmusic.ca/2026/11/23/brenda-lee-surprised-by-taylor-swift-with-diamond-plaque-for-iconic-holiday-hitrockin-around-the-christmas-treesurpassing-10-million-units/">Universal Music Canada</a>. The song, written by Marks and produced by Bradley, was released in 1958 as a single from Lee's album <em>Merry Christmas from Brenda Lee</em>. It reached No. 1 on the Billboard Hot 100 for the first time in 2023, making her the oldest artist ever to top the chart, and it has recently re-entered the chart at No. 30. Lee, the first woman inducted into both the Rock and Roll and Country Music Halls of Fame, turns 82 on 11 December. The <a href="https://growentix.cloud/popmusic">Pop Music</a> hub has the rest of the week's chart news, plus our guide to the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/christmas-number-one-2026-wham-mariah-sam-fender-20261123">2026 Christmas No. 1 race</a>, tracking the festive songs climbing the charts.</p>

<h2>What the Taylor Swift Brenda Lee moment means</h2>

<p>The surprise was not a random celebrity drop-in. Swift has admired Lee for years: she wrote an essay about her at age 18, titled "Rare Peer", which was published in the 2017 book <em>Woman Walk the Line</em>, and she has performed Lee's 1960 hit "I'm Sorry". Lee keeps an autographed guitar from Swift at home. The Diamond award itself is rare air — only Mariah Carey's "All I Want for Christmas Is You", certified Diamond in 2021, had done it before among Christmas songs, and Lee's 1958 recording got there 68 years after it was made. In 2024, Spotify presented Lee with a plaque for reaching 1 billion streams, and the song is now nearing 1.5 billion streams on Spotify alone. The moment also caps a busy Nashville stretch for Swift, who attended her Nashville Songwriters Hall of Fame induction in October and returned to the CMA Awards stage in November for the first time in 13 years.</p>

<h2>What the sources do not say</h2>

<p>Nothing in the report indicates whether Swift and Lee intend to perform or record together, or whether Lee will be at any of this year's Christmas events. The sources don't give an exact certification date for the Diamond award, just that the plaque was awarded on 16th November. They also don't state how the song is currently performing on this week's US streaming charts beyond its Hot 100 at No.30.</p>

<p>Sources: <a href="https://people.com/brenda-lee-gets-emotional-taylor-swift-presents-diamond-plaque-rockin-around-the-christmas-tree-12274708">People</a>, <a href="https://www.universalmusic.ca/2026/11/23/brenda-lee-surprised-by-taylor-swift-with-diamond-plaque-for-iconic-holiday-hitrockin-around-the-christmas-treesurpassing-10-million-units/">Universal Music Canada</a>, <a href="https://www.udiscovermusic.com/news/brenda-lees-rockin-around-the-christmas-tree-diamond-certification/">uDiscover Music</a>.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>Why did Taylor Swift surprise Brenda Lee?</h3>
<p>Swift handed Lee an RIAA Diamond plaque for "Rockin' Around the Christmas Tree" (which had passed 10m in the US) during a surprise visit to Nashville on 16 November 2026.</p>
<h3>How old was Brenda Lee when she recorded the song?</h3>
<p>13 years old in 1958. The song first reached No. 1 on the Hot 100 in 2023, making her the oldest artist ever to top the chart.</p>
