VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'apple-intelligence-usage-packs-20261125', 'tech-ai', 'USA',
'Apple Intelligence Usage Packs Cost $49.99 for Logic Pro',
'Apple Intelligence Usage Packs Cost $49.99 for Logic Pro',
'Apple Intelligence usage packs let Logic Pro users buy extra AI allowance for $49.99, with monthly limits coming to Siri and Image Playground in 2027.',
'Apple Intelligence usage packs let Logic Pro users buy extra AI allowance for $49.99, with monthly limits coming to Siri and Image Playground in 2027.',
$$<p>Apple Intelligence usage packs let Logic Pro users buy extra AI allowance for $49.99 once they exhaust their monthly limit, Apple has confirmed through its support pages. The one-time purchase is the first time Apple has charged directly for additional AI usage, and monthly limits are coming to Siri and Image Playground in 2027.</p>

<table>
<tr><td>Company</td><td>Apple</td></tr>
<tr><td>Product</td><td>Intelligence Usage Packs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Price</td><td>$49.99, one-time purchase, not a subscription</td></tr>
<tr><td>Available now</td><td>Logic Pro, for Creator Studio subscribers</td></tr>
<tr><td>Coming next</td><td>Final Cut Pro, Pixelmator Pro and the iWork suite</td></tr>
<tr><td>Unused usage</td><td>Rolls over monthly, expires 12 months after purchase</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wider limits</td><td>Server-based features including Siri AI from 2027 releases</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>What happened</h2>

<p>Apple have started selling Intelligence Usage Packs in Logic Pro (the music production app). When a Creator Studio subscriber has used up the monthly allowance of the app's AI assistant, a 'Buy More Usage' option appears under Intelligence Features, then Show Usage in the menu bar. The only option is a one-off $49.99 Usage Pack (as per the <a href="https://turbo.gadgets360.com/en/ai/apple-introduces-paid-ai-usage-packs-for-logic-pro-more-apps-to-follow-news-12308768">Gadgets360</a> report on a 9to5Mac report). The packs were introduced in the November update of Logic Pro and <a href="https://turbo.gadgets360.com/en/ai/apple-introduces-paid-ai-usage-packs-for-logic-pro-more-apps-to-follow-news-12308768">Gadgets360</a> reported on that story on 23 November 2026.</p>

<p>The terms are very specific. The packs are tied to the Apple Account that was used to purchase them and cannot be shared via Family Sharing. Purchased usage is only drawn on once the regular monthly allowance has been used up, any unused usage rolls over month on month and any usage that remains at the end of the 12 month period will expire. Apple don't say how much extra assistant time a pack will actually give you and they make no guarantees as to the amount of output you'll get from a given pack will produce a specific amount of output.</p>

<p>Logic Pro is just the beginning. Apple are expected to roll out the packs to the other Creator Studio apps in their November updates (Final Cut Pro, Pixelmator Pro and the iWork suite) with the terms already including Motion, Compressor, MainStage and Freeform as covered apps. The monthly allowances are published per feature (in Keynote you can generate at least 50 presentations and presenter notes for 700 slides a month. The Logic Pro assistant is running on Google's Gemini models and the Keynote Generate Presentation is on OpenAI (as per Apple's support page).</p>

<p>The major change comes next year. An Apple support note states that from the 2027 software releases onwards, usage limits will be applied to the server-based Apple Intelligence features (Siri AI, Image Playground, the Clean Up photo tool and the cloud foundation models in Shortcuts) and that increased access to these features will be available for a fee. A separate report from the iOS 27.3 beta already shows a Siri AI daily usage limit, with a prompt to upgrade your iCloud+ plan after approximately 40 requests in a day.</p>

<h2>What the Apple Intelligence usage packs mean</h2>

<p>This is Apple drawing a line it's avoided for two years. Up until now Apple has positioned Apple Intelligence as a benefit bundled into the hardware margins and the $12.99/month Creator Studio subscription. The $49.99 top-up (which is nearly four times the cost of the monthly subscription) buys you an unspecified amount of extra use and turns AI into a metered utility within Apple's own apps.</p>

<p>The design is very mild for now: it only bites within the professional creative apps, only after you've used up your free monthly allowance, only for subscribers in the eight countries (us, UK, Canada, India etc) on a Mac with Apple Silicon running macOS 27 in US English. The 2027 support note is the real clue though. Once Siri, Image Playground and Clean Up are all metered, the same pay for more model will apply to every iPhone user, not just Logic Pro subscribers. The Siri bit is of course linked to our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/apple-ios-27-3-beta-2-siri-iphone-duo-20261118">iOS 27.3 beta and Siri</a> coverage and there's more on the wider picture in our <a href="https://growentix.cloud/tech-ai">Tech News</a>.</p>

<h2>What the sources do not say</h2>

<p>Apple have published no standalone press release on the packs and the numbers come from the support pages (as per 9to5Mac, Gadgets360 and others) so the launch date is based on the reports not an Apple press release. The sources don't say how much assistant time or how many outputs the $49.99 pack actually gives you and Apple makes no guarantees as to any specific amount of output. The sources don't say what the 2027 fees for Siri or Image Playground will be either or what the free monthly limits will be for those features. The iOS 27.3 Siri limit is a beta find, not a shipped feature and Apple have not confirmed it.</p>

<p>Sources: <a href="https://turbo.gadgets360.com/en/ai/apple-introduces-paid-ai-usage-packs-for-logic-pro-more-apps-to-follow-news-12308768">Gadgets360</a> for the price, Logic Pro availability, the apps to follow and the 2027 limits; <a href="https://www.martincid.com/technology-sv/apple-intelligence-usage-packs-50-logic-pro-ai-limit/">Martin Cid</a> for the country availability, rollover and expiry terms, the monthly allowances and the Gemini and OpenAI model split.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

<h3>How much is an Apple Intelligence Usage Pack?</h3>
<p>One pack is $49.99 as a one off purchase (not a subscription). It's available to Logic Pro for Creator Studio subscribers and you're only charged for usage once your monthly allowance has been used up.</p>

<h3>Will Siri cost money in 2027?</h3>
<p>Apple have not announced a price. Their support note states that usage limits will apply to server based features (including Siri AI from the 2027 software releases) and that enhanced access will be available for a fee. The free allowance and the fee are not yet specified.</p>
$$,
